{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01FJRwFLTfAgQg8STTTvQ9oe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a complete picture. Let me analyze the experiment plan and generate worst-tier predictions for each planned/in_progress experiment. Let me organize all planned experiments:\n\n**Planned experiments:**\n1. c6_libero_suite_vtr - VTR compression on Spatial/Goal/Long\n2. c1_pi05_immune_confirmation - π0.5 immune-class confirmation\n3. c3_oft_graded_full - OFT graded-class full eval\n4. c5_third_connector_roboflamingo - Perceiver Resampler\n\n\n5. c4_learned_reencoding_smolvla - mostly complete, VTR M-sweep\n6. c4_ext_method_universality_openvla - VTR on OpenVLA (already failed)\n7. c4_ext_openvla_msweep - OpenVLA VTC M-sweep\n8. c1_xvla_threshold_localization - X-VLA cliff localization\n9. diagnostic_oft_cv - OFT CV measurement\n10. c6_libero_suite_expansion - Cross-suite expansion\n\nFor the worst-tier predictions, I'm focusing on the key assumption that π0.5 cross-class performance will be the limiting factor across most experiments.\n\nBut the data is pushing back hard on several fronts: token-independent connectors are still getting massive amplification gains on Goal and Long tasks, which breaks the independence assumption I was relying on. The CV scaling law doesn't hold cross-suite either—the gap between R and L2 varies by more than 15 percentage points depending on which suite we're looking at. Then there's the attention pruning result showing X-VLA can be pruned down to k=0.5 while maintaining 99%+ success rate, which undermines the whole narrative about entangling connectors being unprunable. VTR itself looks SmolVLA-specific, and that dip at M=96 suggests training instability. Reviewers are also pointing out that if attention pruning actually solves the X-VLA problem, then my Axis-1 definition was probably flawed to begin with.\n\nI need to shift away from trying to defend a principled two-axis framework and instead lean into this as a comprehensive empirical study that documents what's actually happening across these different configurations.\n\nLooking at the metric ranges I'm tracking, I'm seeing amplification effects ranging from 3 to 15 percentage points, CV strategy correlations between 0.3 and 0.6, cross-suite framework accuracy only hitting 50-75%, and only 2-3 claims surviving review scrutiny. The VTR recovery ratio on SmolVLA is between 0.85 and 0.95, and that pruning gap at k=0.5 is somewhere in the 10-25 percentage point range.\n\nNow I need to think carefully about what \"worst case\" actually means for each experiment, because the data I've already collected shows some genuinely anomalous patterns—like that π0.5 random result where Goal hits 62.2% but Object drops to 9%, which is exactly the kind of breakdown that suggests the two-axis framework is oversimplified. The CV approach fails as a universal predictor, and the paper needs to acknowledge these limitations rather than paper over them.\n\nLooking at what's actually been run versus what's still planned, many of these experiments are already complete or substantially in progress with real data. The worst-case predictions should focus on what the remaining experiments would reveal and how the overall narrative needs to shift to account for these edge cases and failures. I'm looking at the in-progress and planned experiments to generate predictions for the ones still missing data. For the ones that are complete, I already have the results. Let me work through the remaining cases—starting with the in-progress ones that need worst-case tier estimates based on what I've seen so far.\n\nFor c4_learned_reencoding_smolvla, most data is in but there's a concerning dip at M=96 with marginal significance, suggesting potential training instability. The worst case would show high variance across seeds and weaker cross-suite performance, putting VTR recovery at 85-95% of baseline. The OpenVLA universality test already failed completely at M=128, and if the VTC-only variants also fail or show minimal gains, that would confirm VTR is specific to SmolVLA rather than a general technique. The broader M-sweep on OpenVLA is still training, but worst-case would be consistent 0% success rates across all values. For the threshold localization work, the non-monotonic pattern is already emerging in the k-sweep, which undermines the clean cliff hypothesis and suggests the behavior is messier and more model-dependent than expected. The OFT diagnostic is still collecting cross-validation data.\n\nFor the LIBERO suite expansion, I'm seeing unexpected amplification effects—π0.5 is showing surprisingly high performance on Goal and Long tasks even with random k=0.9, which contradicts the assumption that the connector should be independent of task complexity. X-VLA shows variable performance across suites, though attention pruning appears to stabilize it. The planned VTR work on Spatial/Goal/Long tasks will test whether recovery holds across different suite types.\n\nLooking at the π0.5 immunity confirmation, I actually have substantial data already collected in the registry. The key finding is that π0.5 is definitely not immune to the connector method—random k=0.9 causes catastrophic failure on Object tasks (9-10%) but somehow achieves 62.2% on Goal tasks with the same connector and method. This inconsistency breaks the framework because the same linear connector and random method should behave consistently across task types, yet I'm seeing a massive gap between Object and Goal performance.\n\nFor OFT grading, I can't evaluate on LIBERO due to GPU constraints, and I'm stuck with only CV and entropy metrics since OFT remains inaccessible—this is a gap the reviewers will flag.\n\nThe RoboFlamingo connector with Perceiver Resampler fine-tuning is risky because even if the fine-tuning succeeds, it doesn't fit cleanly into the 2-axis taxonomy, which would undermine the framework itself.\n\nNow I need to organize these findings into the YAML output with specific expectations...\n\nLooking at the π0.5 data I've already collected, the results are striking: Object baseline sits at 98.2%, but Random k=0.9 drops catastrophically to around 9-10%, while L2norm k=0.9 maintains 98.2% perfectly. The pattern holds across different k values—Random k=0.95 recovers to 71-74%, but k=0.85 plummets to 5%. For the cross-suite Spatial baseline at 97.2%, Random k=0.9 performs much better at 54.6%, suggesting the vulnerability isn't uniform across task types.\n\nNow I'm examining the Goal baseline results at 96.4%, where Random k=0.9 achieves 62.2%, Random k=0.95 reaches 82.6-83.8%, and L2norm k=0.9 lands in the 88.6-90.6% range. The data cuts off partway through the L2norm k=0.5 Goal results, but the pattern is becoming clearer: L2norm perturbations are consistently more robust than Random ones across all three task suites.\n\nLooking at the Long baseline at 92.8%, the results show a wider spread—Random k=0.9 drops significantly to 31.8-32%, while L2norm k=0.9 maintains 80%. The L2norm variants generally preserve performance better, though Random k=0.7 and L2norm k=0.7 show more comparable results in the 62-68.6% range.\n\nContinuing down to lower k values, Random k=0.5 falls to 46.8% while L2norm k=0.5 stays around 50.2-51.4%, and at k=0.3 both methods degrade further. The critical finding here is that Object tasks show a 53 percentage point gap compared to Goal at k=0.9 with random pruning—this contradicts the token-independent framework's prediction that Object should be more robust. The mechanism appears to be that Object requires fine-grained visual feature discrimination for precise identity matching, which random pruning disrupts more severely than Goal tasks.\n\nThis reveals that task complexity doesn't just amplify entangling connectors—it creates inverted amplification patterns for independent connectors too, where simpler Object tasks become harder to prune randomly while complex Goal tasks remain easier. This breaks the assumption that token-independent connectors should be immune to task complexity effects. Looking at attention pruning results on X-VLA, Object at k=0.5 shows near-perfect retention across all attention mechanisms, suggesting attention-based pruning behaves fundamentally differently from token pruning. Looking at the performance metrics, attention-based pruning dramatically outperforms L2-norm across all test suites—even at k=0.5, X-VLA maintains >88% success rate compared to L2-norm's 42.6% on Object tasks. This suggests the real issue isn't token entanglement itself, but that L2-norm is fundamentally the wrong importance metric, which actually undermines the core claim that token coupling determines prunability since attention-based pruning makes X-VLA nearly as prunable as π0. Now checking the π0.5 attention pruning results to see if this pattern holds there too.\n\nThe π0.5 model tells a different story—attention pruning works well at high k values (98.4% at k=0.95, 97.2% at k=0.9) but catastrophically fails at k=0.7 on Object tasks (0.6% success), whereas X-VLA remained robust across all k values. This suggests attention-based pruning isn't universally solving the problem; it's model-dependent, which complicates the narrative considerably.\n\nNow I'm looking at the planned and in-progress experiments to prioritize which ones to predict on—there's a mix of VTR studies on different model variants, threshold localization work for X-VLA, OFT measurements, and cross-suite expansion tests that will help clarify where these pruning methods actually generalize. other suites. Let me focus on what the worst-tier interpretation of all this data would look like, both what's already collected and what's still to come.\n\nThe user wants detailed predictions for each planned experiment in the experiment plan. Looking at what's marked as planned or in-progress, I need to generate worst-tier predictions for all of them. For experiments with existing data, I'll extrapolate what the remaining results would show to fit the worst narrative. The core story here is that metric selection matters more than connector architecture, cross-suite validation fails, and VTR performance plateaus with SmolVLA.\n\nNow I'm writing up the YAML specification for each experiment with careful attention to structure. For each one I need to define the name, plan ID, description, expected results with metrics, the rationale for those results, what tables and figures would show, and the analysis that ties it together. Let me work through the LIBERO suite expansion carefully since it has the most data already collected.\n\nThe random pruning results across suites reveal a critical tension in my framework—the 53 percentage point gap between Object and Goal performance at k=0.9 shouldn't exist if token-independent connectors truly behave uniformly across tasks, but L2norm shows much tighter cross-suite consistency with only around 18 percentage points of variation, suggesting the framework holds better for norm-based methods than random selection.\n\nLooking at the worst tier performance, the gap between random and L2norm reverses on long-horizon tasks—L2norm actually outperforms random on Long while random dominates on Object, Spatial, and Goal—which means the coefficient of variation scaling law I thought was universal breaks down depending on task horizon, and I need to check whether the rank correlation between CV and the random-versus-L2norm performance delta holds consistently across suites or if it's task-dependent. how consistent it is across suites...\n\nActually, the scaling law is about comparing ACROSS models (π0.5 CV=0.055, X-VLA CV=0.151, OpenVLA CV=0.215) within the same suite. The worst tier says this relationship weakens cross-suite.\n\nAt k=0.5, I'm seeing the monotonic pattern hold for Object, Spatial, and Goal—lower CV correlates with larger positive deltas—but it breaks down on Long. There, π0.5 has the lowest CV yet shows a negative delta, while X-VLA jumps to +17, which violates the expected ordering. The L2norm reversal in π0.5 on Long is the culprit, suggesting the monotonic relationship doesn't universally hold across all task types. I'm realizing there's a discrepancy in how the axis2_amplification metric is defined. The worst tier specifies a range of [3, 15]pp, but the actual data from π0.5 shows a 53pp difference between Goal and Object conditions with random k=0.9, which far exceeds that range. This suggests either the metric is measuring something different than I initially understood, or the definition needs clarification—the core issue is whether this massive amplification actually violates the assumption that token-independent connectors shouldn't be affected by task complexity. I'm realizing that token-independent connectors also show significant amplification on the Goal/Long task, which means the amplification effect isn't unique to entangling connectors. So the [3, 15]pp range might actually represent the incremental amplification gain from being an entangling connector rather than independent. Let me check the math: if entangling connectors drop 27.4pp and independent ones drop 9.6pp, the difference would be around 17.8pp—which fits within or near that range.\n\nThe comparison gets messier when I look at random versus L2norm metrics, since the direction of effects differs. I think the core insight is that the axis2_amplification_pp range of [3, 15]pp represents the net amplification specifically attributable to the entangling versus independent distinction, which is smaller than the claimed ~27pp because independent connectors themselves show substantial cross-suite variation.\n\nRather than overanalyze further, I should structure the output around the worst tier predictions. For each experiment, I need to lay out the expected numerical results, explain the underlying mechanisms in the worst tier context, and present this through tables and analysis that form a coherent narrative. The five planned experiments should cover suite expansion effects, VTR generalization weakness, π0.5's lack of immunity to method×task interactions, OFT's limited data, and how Perceiver Resampler doesn't fit the taxonomy.\n\nNow I'm working through the remaining experiments—VTR's high variance issues, OpenVLA's complete failure modes, X-VLA's method-dependent cliff behavior, and the CV/OpenVLA comparison that can't evaluate SR. I notice E5 attention pruning has existing data but isn't formally in the experiment plan, so I need to verify whether it should be included in the registry or treated separately.\n\nLooking at the attention pruning results for π0.5 and OpenVLA, I can see the performance degradation curves across different sparsity levels—π0.5 shows a sharp cliff at k=0.7 with catastrophic failure, while the other tasks maintain more graceful degradation, and OpenVLA's pruning behavior appears to follow a different pattern. Looking at the X-VLA results, attention pruning is dramatically outperforming both L2norm and random baselines across all metrics—Object detection at 99.2%, Spatial at 88.8%, Long-horizon at 94%, and Goal at 98.2%. This suggests the core issue wasn't token entanglement but rather using the wrong importance metric for pruning. Now I'm moving on to write out the YAML configuration for the experiment plans.\n\nI need to clarify what the user is asking for—they want predictions for all non-completed experiments, whether they're marked as planned or in-progress. For the in-progress ones with existing data, I'll predict what the remaining outcomes would show and provide an overall interpretation under the worst-tier assumption. I'll organize everything by plan_id and skip the abandoned c7_libero_plus_robustness experiment.\n\nWriting YAML predictions... Now I'm working through the specific performance predictions for the cross-suite expansion experiments, starting with the OpenVLA baseline and pruning results across different task suites to establish what numbers I'd expect to see. 8pp (random better!). So OpenVLA shows the opposite pattern—L2norm wins on Object but random dominates on Goal. This contradicts the idea that coefficient of variation alone predicts which method performs better. Looking at the worst tier results across all suites with k=0.5, I'm seeing that OpenVLA's preference flips depending on the benchmark, even though its CV stays constant at 0.215.\n\nThe variation is striking: OpenVLA ranges from -1.8 to +8.8 across suites, while π0.5 swings from +36 to -4.6—a 40 percentage point spread. This tells me the method preference isn't determined by CV universally; it's fundamentally task-dependent. When I look at the Spearman correlation between CV and the method difference across suites, it's perfectly monotonic on Object tasks but breaks down elsewhere, suggesting CV is only predictive within specific benchmark domains.\n\nNow I'm assembling the comprehensive YAML output and calculating what fraction of the suite-model-k combinations the two-axis framework actually predicts correctly.\n\nLooking at how well the framework performs: SmolVLA's predictions align perfectly with the observed catastrophic collapse across all suites, but X-VLA shows mixed results where the framework's task-dependent collapse hypothesis only partially holds—Object suite stays robust while Goal suite does collapse. For π0.5, the framework's immunity prediction breaks down depending on the method, suggesting the framework captures some patterns but misses method-specific interactions.\n\nWhen I evaluate which claims survive scrutiny, the 2-axis framework itself fails as a principled explanation and downgrades to just describing empirical observations with exceptions. The pixel-shuffle entanglement claim holds up well since SmolVLA's cliff is consistent and universal, while the connector-specific patterns survive only as loose empirical observations rather than principled predictions. VTR works but only for SmolVLA specifically, not as a general mechanism.\n\nNow I'm checking the pi05_l2norm_random_gap metric more carefully—the definition specifies a gap between L2norm and random at k=0.5 should fall in the [10, 25] range, but my measurements show L2norm at 33.4% versus random at 69.4%, giving a 36pp gap that's well outside the expected bounds.\n\nHowever, looking at the cross-suite average tells a different story: Object contributes +36pp, but Spatial adds +16pp, Goal adds +13.8pp, and Long actually subtracts 4.6pp, which averages to about 15pp across all suites—right in the target range. So the 36pp on Object is an outlier, and the metric's [10, 25] threshold likely refers to the typical cross-suite average rather than individual suite performance.\n\nNow I'm ready to write up the full output, and I should also consider how the E5 attention pruning results on X-VLA fit into the broader picture.\n\nThe E5 results are actually quite damaging to the paper's core argument. When using attention-based importance instead of norm-based importance, X-VLA achieves near-perfect selectivity at k=0.5 across all suites, which suggests the \"entanglement\" property isn't inherent to the connector architecture itself—it's an artifact of how importance is measured. This undermines the paper's claim that the connector design is the primary determinant of pruning behavior; the real factor is the choice of importance metric. A reviewer could argue that the paper is conflating connector architecture with susceptibility to L2 norm selection bias, and that with the right metric, entangling connectors become just as prunable as others.\n\nFor the VTR experiments, I'm looking at the recovery ratio metrics.  The current data shows 56-62% success rate versus the 59.2% baseline, which puts us at the high end of the expected 0.85-0.95 recovery range. Cross-suite results are mixed: Object recovers at 1.01x baseline, Spatial actually exceeds baseline at 1.19x, and Goal sits at 0.93x. If the Long suite data comes in around 0.85x, the average would still be within acceptable bounds, though the variance across suites is concerning.\n\nThe M=96 dip with p=0.034 is a red flag for training instability, and VTR's flat performance curve across model sizes suggests there could be a non-trivial failure mode lurking. Now I need to write out the YAML configuration and verify which experiments are actually planned versus already in progress—looks like four are planned and three are currently running.\n\nI should generate predictions for all of them using the existing data to inform the remaining ones, keeping the worst-tier narrative consistent throughout. I'm also noting that E5 attention pruning results should inform the analysis even though they're not explicitly in the experiment plan itself. Let me focus on what the user asked for and stick to the planned entries while weaving E5 findings into the broader analysis.\n\nActually, I'm realizing some of these \"planned\" experiments may have already been substantially executed based on the registry data, so I need to double-check their actual status before writing predictions.\n\nNow I'm structuring the YAML output carefully to avoid parsing issues with flow sequences and quoted strings. For each experiment, I'm predicting what the remaining gaps would show and how the full dataset would be interpreted under the worst-tier framework.\n\nFor c6_libero_suite_expansion, I'm expecting cross-suite data to reveal framework fragility with massive method×task interactions and significant drops in cross-suite scaling law correlations. For c1_pi05_immune_confirmation, I'm predicting that π0.5 is not actually immune to the performance cliff, particularly at the Object task level.\n\nFor c6_libero_suite_vtr, VTR recovery weakens on Goal and Long tasks with a reproducible dip at M=96, suggesting it's specific to SmolVLA rather than generalizable. For c3_oft_graded_full, OFT evaluation remains blocked by GPU incompatibility, with the paper's claims relying only on entropy and CV comparisons. For c5_third_connector_roboflamingo, fine-tuning produces low baseline performance and the Perceiver Resampler doesn't fit cleanly into the framework, so it's dropped from the paper.\n\nNow looking at the reencoding results: VTR works but shows a real dip at M=96 with high seed variance across some M values, indicating it's reliable but training-sensitive. When testing VTC-only configurations with OpenVLA at M=32 and M=64, both fail with near-zero success rates, confirming VTR is SmolVLA-specific. Across all M values with the MLP projector, success rates are near-zero, so VTR doesn't generalize there either. For the XVLA threshold localization, there's a clear cliff at k=0.85 with 68% success rate and minimal variance across seeds, though the relationship becomes non-monotonic below that threshold.\n\nThe attention pruning approach eliminates this cliff entirely, which is interesting. Meanwhile, the OFT diagnostic shows a coefficient of variation matching OpenVLA at 0.219±0.01, confirming the connector determines this metric, though I don't have success rate data for that experiment yet.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1043,"cache_read_input_tokens":127511,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1043},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0a5ab60b-18ac-4b1d-b58b-ab75725b2ce1","uuid":"9f0cc589-f712-4d01-9ec6-a7de43945d5d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01FJRwFLTfAgQg8STTTvQ9oe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have the full experiment plan. Let me cross-reference with the existing registry data to generate worst-tier predictions.\n\n```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  核心 reframe：从 'principled 2-axis framework' 转为 'comprehensive empirical study of VLA token pruning across architectures and tasks'。\n  π0.5 cross-suite 数据摧毁了两轴独立性假设——random k=0.9 在 Object=9% vs Goal=62.2%，同一 token-independent connector 跨 suite 差异达 53pp。\n  E5 attention pruning 数据（X-VLA k=0.5 attn_last=99.2% vs L2norm=42.6%）证明 'entanglement' 不是 connector 的固有属性，而是 importance metric 选择的 artifact。\n  CV scaling law 仅在 Object suite 内部成立（Spearman ρ=-1.0），跨 suite 后 Long-horizon 出现反转（π0.5 L2norm > random），平均 |ρ|≈0.45。\n  VTR 确认为 SmolVLA-specific 方案（OpenVLA VTC-only 全部失败），且 M=96 dip (p=0.034) 暗示训练不稳定。\n  Title 改为 'A Systematic Study of Token Pruning Strategies Across VLA Architectures'。\n  仍然 submit CoRL，因为 5 models × 4 suites × systematic comparison 是 substantial empirical contribution。\n  Claims 缩减为：(1) pixel-shuffle entanglement 是真实的架构属性（C2 survives），(2) importance metric 选择 > connector architecture（new empirical finding），(3) VTR 在 pixel-shuffle 上实现 near-lossless compression（C4 survives as case study）。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  - name: \"Cross-Suite Expansion: π0.5 + X-VLA + OpenVLA + SmolVLA × 4 Suites\"\n    plan_id: \"c6_libero_suite_expansion\"\n    description: >\n      将所有 5 models 的 pruning 实验从 Object 扩展到 Spatial/Goal/Long。\n      核心目的：验证 2-axis framework 的 cross-suite 一致性。\n      实际结果：framework 在 Object suite 上准确，但 cross-suite 后出现系统性偏差。\n    expected_results:\n      pi05_random_k09_object_sr_pct: 9.3\n      pi05_random_k09_goal_sr_pct: 62.2\n      pi05_random_k09_spatial_sr_pct: 54.0\n      pi05_random_k09_long_sr_pct: 31.4\n      pi05_random_k09_cross_suite_range_pp: 52.9\n      pi05_l2norm_k09_object_sr_pct: 98.2\n      pi05_l2norm_k09_goal_sr_pct: 89.6\n      pi05_l2norm_k09_spatial_sr_pct: 95.3\n      pi05_l2norm_k09_long_sr_pct: 80.0\n      pi05_l2norm_k09_cross_suite_range_pp: 18.2\n      xvla_l2norm_k09_object_sr_pct: 97.6\n      xvla_l2norm_k09_goal_sr_pct: 70.2\n      xvla_l2norm_k09_spatial_sr_pct: 78.8\n      xvla_l2norm_k09_long_sr_pct: 27.5\n      xvla_l2norm_k095_long_sr_pct: 47.0\n      smolvla_k095_all_suites_sr_pct: \"<0.1 (all 4 suites)\"\n      cv_strategy_spearman_object: -1.0\n      cv_strategy_spearman_goal: -0.5\n      cv_strategy_spearman_long: 0.5\n      cv_strategy_abs_spearman_mean: 0.45\n      delta_R_L2_k05_pi05_object_pp: 36.0\n      delta_R_L2_k05_pi05_goal_pp: 13.8\n      delta_R_L2_k05_pi05_long_pp: -4.6\n      delta_R_L2_k05_xvla_object_pp: 28.0\n      delta_R_L2_k05_xvla_goal_pp: 8.5\n      delta_R_L2_k05_xvla_long_pp: 17.0\n      delta_R_L2_k05_openvla_object_pp: -1.8\n      delta_R_L2_k05_openvla_goal_pp: 8.8\n      framework_accuracy_pct: 62\n      axis2_amplification_entangling_minus_independent_pp: 11.4\n      e5_xvla_attn_last_k05_object_sr_pct: 99.2\n      e5_xvla_attn_last_k05_goal_sr_pct: 98.2\n      e5_xvla_attn_last_k05_spatial_sr_pct: 88.8\n      e5_xvla_attn_last_k05_long_sr_pct: 90.2\n      e5_xvla_attn_mean_k05_long_sr_pct: 94.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      π0.5 random k=0.9 在 Object 上出现 catastrophic cliff（9.3%），但在 Goal 上仅下降至 62.2%——同一 linear projection connector、同一 random method、同一 k，仅 task distribution 不同就产生 53pp 差异。这直接破坏 \"token-independent connector 不受 task complexity 影响\" 的核心假设。\n      机制：Object suite 需要 precise object identity discrimination（visually similar condiments），random 在 cliff zone 摧毁 concentrated discriminative features；Goal suite 的 task 由 language instruction 区分，vision tokens 冗余度更高，random 破坏的影响小。\n      L2norm 在相同 k=0.9 的 cross-suite range 仅 18.2pp（vs random 53pp），证明 cross-suite sensitivity 是 METHOD-dependent 而非 connector-dependent。\n      E5 attention pruning 数据更具破坏性：X-VLA k=0.5 attn_last=99.2%（Object）、98.2%（Goal），vs L2norm=42.6%/59%。这意味着 X-VLA 的 \"entanglement\" 问题完全可以通过更换 importance metric 解决，BART encoder 产生的不是 \"irreversible entanglement\" 而是 \"norm-unfriendly importance distribution\"。\n      CV scaling law 在 Object 内仍然成立（Spearman -1.0），但 Long-horizon 出现反转（π0.5 L2norm > random，Δ=-4.6pp），导致 cross-suite 平均 |ρ|≈0.45，远低于 paper 声称的 \"universal predictor\" 所需的 >0.8。\n      OpenVLA 在 Goal 上也出现 method preference reversal（random > L2norm +8.8pp），而 Object 上 L2norm > random（+1.8pp）。同一 CV=0.215 的 model，跨 suite 后 method preference 反转。\n      Framework 在 20 个 model×suite 预测中仅正确约 12 个（62%），达不到 \"principled framework\" 标准。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table A: Cross-Suite Δ(Random-L2norm) at k=0.5 — CV Scaling Law Breakdown\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"CV\", \"Object Δ(pp)\", \"Spatial Δ(pp)\", \"Goal Δ(pp)\", \"Long Δ(pp)\", \"Range(pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"π0.5\", \"0.055\", \"+36.0\", \"+16.0\", \"+13.8\", \"-4.6\", \"40.6\"]\n          - [\"X-VLA\", \"0.151\", \"+28.0\", \"+12.6\", \"+8.5\", \"+17.0\", \"19.5\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"0.215\", \"-1.8\", \"~+5\", \"+8.8\", \"~+3\", \"~10.6\"]\n        notes: \"Object suite 上 monotonic（ρ=-1.0），Long suite 上 π0.5 reversal 破坏 monotonicity。Cross-suite mean |ρ|≈0.45。\"\n      - title: \"Table B: π0.5 Random k=0.9 Cross-Suite — Token-Independent ≠ Task-Independent\"\n        columns: [\"Suite\", \"Baseline(%)\", \"Random k=0.9(%)\", \"Δ from baseline(pp)\", \"L2norm k=0.9(%)\", \"Method gap(pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Object\", \"98.2\", \"9.3\", \"-88.9\", \"98.2\", \"-88.9\"]\n          - [\"Spatial\", \"97.2\", \"54.0\", \"-43.2\", \"95.3\", \"-41.3\"]\n          - [\"Goal\", \"96.4\", \"62.2\", \"-34.2\", \"89.6\", \"-27.4\"]\n          - [\"Long\", \"92.8\", \"31.4\", \"-61.4\", \"80.0\", \"-12.8\"]\n        notes: \"Cross-suite range 53pp for random vs 18pp for L2norm。Task sensitivity 是 method-specific，非 architecture-level property。\"\n      - title: \"Table C: E5 Attention Pruning Demolishes Entanglement Narrative (X-VLA k=0.5)\"\n        columns: [\"Suite\", \"L2norm(%)\", \"Random(%)\", \"Attn-Last(%)\", \"Attn-Mean(%)\", \"Best Attn vs L2norm(pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Object\", \"42.6\", \"70.6\", \"99.2\", \"98.4\", \"+56.6\"]\n          - [\"Spatial\", \"58.8\", \"71.4\", \"88.8\", \"91.6\", \"+32.8\"]\n          - [\"Goal\", \"59.0\", \"67.2\", \"98.2\", \"97.4\", \"+38.4\"]\n          - [\"Long\", \"44.6\", \"61.6\", \"90.2\", \"94.0\", \"+49.4\"]\n        notes: \"Attention pruning 在所有 4 suites 上实现 88-99% SR at k=0.5。问题不在 connector entanglement，在 importance metric。\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig cross-suite heatmap: 5 models × 4 suites × 2 methods (L2norm/random) at k=0.5/k=0.9, 颜色编码 SR。清晰展示 framework 预测（虚线框）vs 实际结果的 mismatch areas。\"\n      - \"Fig CV vs Δ(R-L2) scatter: 4 panels (one per suite), 每个 panel 3 个点 (π0.5/X-VLA/OpenVLA)，展示 scaling law 在 Object 上线性但在 Long 上崩溃。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cross-suite 数据系统性地破坏 2-axis framework 的两个核心预测：\n      (1) Axis-1 独立性：token-independent connectors should be immune to task complexity → π0.5 random k=0.9 Object=9% vs Goal=62% 证伪（53pp gap）。\n      (2) CV universal predictor：CV 应在所有 suite 上预测 method preference → Long-horizon 上 π0.5 出现 reversal（L2norm > random），OpenVLA 在 Goal 上也 reversal。\n      E5 attention pruning 数据进一步瓦解 Axis-1 定义：X-VLA（\"entangling\"）在 attention pruning 下表现如同 \"independent\" connector。Axis-1 的区分不在 \"token coupling\" 而在 \"susceptibility to norm-based importance bias\"。\n      Reframe：论文不能声称发现了 governing principle，而应定位为 \"comprehensive empirical study revealing that importance metric selection matters more than connector architecture\"。\n\n  - name: \"π0.5 Token-Independent Confirmation (4B, Linear Proj)\"\n    plan_id: \"c1_pi05_immune_confirmation\"\n    description: >\n      π0.5 作为 2nd token-independent data point，验证 CV=0.055 的 linear projection 在所有 suite 上的 pruning 行为。\n      worst 档：π0.5 数据揭示 \"immune class\" 不存在——random pruning 在 cliff zone (k=0.85-0.925) 产生 catastrophic collapse，且行为极度 task-dependent。\n    expected_results:\n      pi05_cv: 0.055\n      pi05_baseline_object_sr_pct: 98.2\n      pi05_baseline_spatial_sr_pct: 97.2\n      pi05_baseline_goal_sr_pct: 96.4\n      pi05_baseline_long_sr_pct: 92.8\n      pi05_random_k095_object_sr_pct: 71.1\n      pi05_random_k0925_object_sr_pct: 27.6\n      pi05_random_k09_object_sr_pct: 10.8\n      pi05_random_k085_object_sr_pct: 5.0\n      pi05_random_k07_object_sr_pct: 75.5\n      pi05_random_k05_object_sr_pct: 69.4\n      pi05_l2norm_k09_object_sr_pct: 98.2\n      pi05_l2norm_k085_object_sr_pct: 98.0\n      pi05_l2norm_k05_object_sr_pct: 33.4\n      pi05_l2norm_k03_object_sr_pct: 51.0\n      pi05_random_cliff_depth_pp: 66.1\n      pi05_l2norm_v_shape_depth_pp: 17.6\n      pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k05_cross_suite_avg_pp: 15.3\n      pi05_attention_k07_object_sr_pct: 0.6\n      pi05_attention_k05_object_sr_pct: 37.8\n      pi05_attention_k095_object_sr_pct: 98.4\n    result_rationale: >\n      π0.5（CV=0.055）本应是 \"immune\" class 的完美验证，但数据揭示了截然不同的图景：\n      (1) Random-specific cliff：k=0.95→71.1% → k=0.925→27.6% → k=0.9→10.8% → k=0.85→5.0%，在 10% keep ratio 变化范围内产生 66pp collapse。这个 cliff 是 random-specific 的——L2norm 在同区间保持 98.0-99.2% 的 plateau。\n      (2) Fixed-mask experiment 排除了 temporal inconsistency（T0=12% = per-call 12%），证明 cliff 是 spatial coverage 的 structural failure。\n      (3) V-shape non-monotonicity：L2norm 在 k=0.5 出现 valley（33.4%），k=0.7=55.0% 和 k=0.3=51.0% 都更高。Token position visualization 确认 k=0.5 恰好是 spatial clustering 最严重的点（1 cluster, 78% coverage）。\n      (4) Cross-suite 数据摧毁 \"immune\" 标签：random k=0.9 在 Object=9% 但 Goal=62.2%（+53pp），Spatial=54%，Long=31.4%。Object 的 concentrated critical features（visually similar condiments）在 cliff zone 极度脆弱，而 Goal 的 language-disambiguated tasks 对 random token loss 更 robust。\n      (5) Attention pruning 不解决问题：k=0.7 attn=0.6%（比 random 的 75.5% 差 75pp），k=0.5 attn=37.8%（与 L2norm 33.4% 持平）。π0.5 的 attention map 不提供有效 importance signal。\n      In worst tier, π0.5 从 \"immune class exemplar\" 降级为 \"case study demonstrating that pruning behavior is an irreducible function of method × k × task, not a simple connector property\"。Cross-suite average Δ(R-L2) at k=0.5 = (+36+16+13.8-4.6)/4 = 15.3pp，远低于 Object-only 的 36pp。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table D: π0.5 Random Cliff Zone (Object Suite)\"\n        columns: [\"k\", \"Tokens kept\", \"Random SR(%)\", \"L2norm SR(%)\", \"Δ(L2-R)(pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0.95\", \"730\", \"71.1\", \"98.2\", \"+27.1\"]\n          - [\"0.925\", \"710\", \"27.6\", \"99.2\", \"+71.6\"]\n          - [\"0.90\", \"691\", \"10.8\", \"98.2\", \"+87.4\"]\n          - [\"0.85\", \"653\", \"5.0\", \"98.0\", \"+93.0\"]\n          - [\"0.70\", \"538\", \"75.5\", \"55.0\", \"-20.5\"]\n          - [\"0.50\", \"384\", \"69.4\", \"33.4\", \"-36.0\"]\n          - [\"0.30\", \"230\", \"36.4\", \"51.0\", \"+14.6\"]\n        notes: \"方法偏好在 k=0.7 附近反转。Cliff zone (k=0.85-0.925) L2norm 完胜；aggressive zone (k=0.5-0.7) random 完胜。\"\n      - title: \"Table E: π0.5 Cross-Suite Random k=0.9 — 'Immune' Class Falsified\"\n        columns: [\"Suite\", \"Baseline(%)\", \"Random k=0.9(%)\", \"L2norm k=0.9(%)\", \"Δ from baseline (random, pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Object\", \"98.2\", \"9.3\", \"98.2\", \"-88.9\"]\n          - [\"Spatial\", \"97.2\", \"54.0\", \"95.3\", \"-43.2\"]\n          - [\"Goal\", \"96.4\", \"62.2\", \"89.6\", \"-34.2\"]\n          - [\"Long\", \"92.8\", \"31.4\", \"80.0\", \"-61.4\"]\n        notes: \"同一 model/method/k，cross-suite range=53pp。Framework 预测 token-independent 应 <5pp variation。\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig π0.5 dual-method pruning curve: x=k, y=SR, two lines (random/L2norm), Object suite。突出 random cliff zone 和 L2norm V-shape valley。\"\n      - \"Fig π0.5 4-suite comparison: 4 panels, 每 panel 一个 suite, random+L2norm curves。展示 cross-suite behavior divergence。\"\n    analysis: >\n      π0.5 数据是 worst 档的 smoking gun：CV=0.055 的 pure linear projection 不 \"immune\"，只是 L2norm 恰好在 cliff zone 有效。\n      换用 random pruning，即出现 catastrophic cliff。换 suite（Goal/Long），random 的 cliff 消失但 L2norm 的 advantage 也缩小。\n      这意味着 \"compressibility\" 不是 connector 的 intrinsic property，而是 (connector, method, k, task) 四元组的 emergent property。\n      2-axis framework 的简化——将其压缩为 (connector, task) 二维——在 worst 档数据下失效。\n      Paper 需要 reframe：不是 \"connector determines compressibility\"，而是 \"we provide the first comprehensive map of the 4D pruning landscape across VLA architectures\"。\n\n  - name: \"VTR Cross-Suite Generalization (SmolVLA M=32 on Spatial/Goal/Long)\"\n    plan_id: \"c6_libero_suite_vtr\"\n    description: >\n      SmolVLA VTR M=32 在 Spatial/Goal/Long suites 上的压缩性能验证。\n      worst 档：VTR cross-suite recovery 衰减，且 VTR 训练在非 Object suite 上有不稳定性。\n    expected_results:\n      vtr_m32_object_sr_pct: 60.1\n      vtr_m32_spatial_sr_pct: 53.2\n      vtr_m32_goal_sr_pct: 56.4\n      vtr_m32_long_sr_pct_predicted: 48.0\n      smolvla_baseline_object_sr_pct: 59.2\n      smolvla_baseline_spatial_sr_pct: 44.6\n      smolvla_baseline_goal_sr_pct: 60.8\n      smolvla_baseline_long_sr_pct: 36.6\n      vtr_recovery_ratio_object: 1.015\n      vtr_recovery_ratio_spatial: 1.193\n      vtr_recovery_ratio_goal: 0.928\n      vtr_recovery_ratio_long_predicted: 0.874\n      vtr_recovery_ratio_mean: 0.95\n      vtr_m96_dip_p_value: 0.034\n      vtr_m96_dip_confirmed: true\n      hard_pruning_k05_all_suites_sr_pct: 0.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      VTR M=32 在 Object 上实现 near-lossless compression（60.1% vs baseline 59.2%），Spatial 上甚至超过 baseline（53.2% vs 44.6%，可能因为 VTR 训练 regularization 效应）。\n      但 Goal suite recovery ratio = 56.4/60.8 = 0.928，低于 Object。预测 Long-horizon（未测）recovery ratio 进一步下降至 ~0.87：Long tasks 需要 multi-step reasoning，VTR 的 cross-attention 可能无法完全保留 temporal action sequence 所需的 spatial information chain。\n      M=96 dip（p=0.034 vs M=64）在 worst 档被确认为 training instability（非 statistical fluke），因为 M=96 的 3-seed std=3.2pp 是所有 M 值中最高的。这暗示 VTR 的 flat M-curve 可能是 M=16-64 的幸运区间，M=96 暴露了 cross-attention query 数量与 pixel-shuffle token structure 之间的 resonance 问题。\n      VTR 仍然是 valid contribution（从 0% hard pruning 恢复到 ~baseline），但 worst 档将其定位为 \"SmolVLA-specific case study\" 而非 \"general method\"，因为：\n      (1) cross-suite recovery 有衰减（Goal 0.93, Long predicted 0.87），\n      (2) M=96 dip 暗示 training sensitivity，\n      (3) OpenVLA VTR 完全失败（下条）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table F: VTR M=32 Cross-Suite Recovery (SmolVLA)\"\n        columns: [\"Suite\", \"Hard Prune k=0.5(%)\", \"VTR M=32(%)\", \"Baseline(%)\", \"Recovery Ratio\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Object\", \"0.0\", \"60.1\", \"59.2\", \"1.015\"]\n          - [\"Spatial\", \"0.6\", \"53.2\", \"44.6\", \"1.193\"]\n          - [\"Goal\", \"0.0\", \"56.4\", \"60.8\", \"0.928\"]\n          - [\"Long (pred)\", \"0.0\", \"~48\", \"36.6\", \"~0.87\"]\n        notes: \"Recovery ratio 从 Object(1.0) 下降到 Long(0.87)。VTR 在 complex tasks 上 recovery 衰减 ~13%。\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig VTR M-curve with error bars: x=M, y=SR, 3-seed error bars。M=96 dip 突出标注 p=0.034。\"\n      - \"Fig VTR cross-suite bar chart: 4 suites × (hard prune / VTR M=32 / baseline)，展示 recovery gap 在 Long 上最大。\"\n    analysis: >\n      VTR 从 \"universal compression method\" 降级为 \"effective recovery tool for pixel-shuffle connectors, with decreasing efficacy on complex tasks\"。\n      M=96 dip 的 statistical significance (p=0.034) 不足以证明 systematic failure（n=3 power ~0.2），但足以引起 reviewer 对 training stability 的质疑。\n      Cross-suite recovery 衰减是合理的：VTR 在 Object suite 上训练，cross-suite 是 zero-shot transfer。Long-horizon tasks 的 action sequence 依赖 precise temporal-spatial correspondence，VTR 的 cross-attention bottleneck 可能丢失这些 long-range dependencies。\n      Paper 策略：VTR 作为 §4.7 的 case study 保留，但移除 \"universal compression\" 措辞，改为 \"recovers pixel-shuffle cliff-edge to near-baseline on trained distribution, with ~13% degradation on out-of-distribution complex tasks\"。\n\n  - name: \"VTR Universality Test: OpenVLA MLP Projector (M=128/32/64)\"\n    plan_id: \"c4_ext_method_universality_openvla\"\n    description: >\n      VTR 在 OpenVLA（MLP projector）上的泛化性测试。M=128 full VTR 已失败（0% SR），VTC-only M=32/M=64 作为 fallback。\n    expected_results:\n      openvla_vtr_m128_sr_pct: 0.0\n      openvla_vtconly_m32_sr_pct_predicted: 3.0\n      openvla_vtconly_m64_sr_pct_predicted: 5.0\n      openvla_vtconly_m96_sr_pct_predicted: 2.0\n      openvla_baseline_sr_pct: 74.0\n      overfitting_confirmed: true\n      failure_mode: \"model outputs identical action every timestep\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      M=128 VTR 在 20K steps 后 0% SR（model 对所有 observation 输出相同 action）确认 severe overfitting。\n      VTC-only M=32/M=64 预测同样失败（<5% SR），因为根本原因不在 VTR architecture 而在 MLP projector tokens 的特性：\n      (1) MLP projector tokens 已经是 individually meaningful 的（CV=0.215, 有 gradient differentiation），VTR 的 cross-attention 无法提供额外信息，反而引入 information bottleneck。\n      (2) OpenVLA 的 256 tokens × 7B parameters 的 scale 与 SmolVLA 的 128 tokens × 450M parameters 完全不同——VTR 的 ~22M params 对 7B model 来说是 rounding error，无法学到有意义的 re-encoding。\n      (3) M=96/M=64/M=32 的 training loss 持续下降但 eval SR 不恢复，典型的 action space overfitting pattern。\n      在 worst 档，这确认 VTR 是 pixel-shuffle-specific method。Paper 中 VTR 需要 reframe：不是 \"universal compression tool\" 而是 \"architecture-specific recovery mechanism that works because pixel-shuffle tokens need re-entangling, while MLP tokens are already independent and don't benefit from cross-attention re-encoding\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table G: VTR on OpenVLA — Universal Failure\"\n        columns: [\"Config\", \"M\", \"Params(M)\", \"Steps\", \"Train Loss\", \"SR(%)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Full VTR\", \"128\", \"22.2\", \"20K\", \"converged\", \"0.0\"]\n          - [\"VTC-only\", \"32\", \"22.2\", \"100K\", \"converged\", \"~3\"]\n          - [\"VTC-only\", \"64\", \"22.2\", \"100K\", \"converged\", \"~5\"]\n          - [\"VTC-only\", \"96\", \"22.2\", \"100K\", \"converged\", \"~2\"]\n          - [\"LoRA baseline\", \"—\", \"883\", \"100K\", \"0.065\", \"0.0\"]\n        notes: \"所有 VTR configs 失败。Train loss 收敛但 SR ≈0。Failure mode: identical action output。\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig overfitting diagnostic: training loss curve (converging) + eval SR curve (flat at 0%), 展示 train/eval disconnect。\"\n    analysis: >\n      VTR universality 完全失败。这不是 hyperparameter tuning 问题——M=128/96/64/32 全部 <5% SR，且 LoRA fine-tuning 也产生 0% SR（libero_lora_baseline），说明 OpenVLA 的 fine-tuning 本身就 fragile。\n      Reviewer 会问：\"如果 VTR 只在 SmolVLA 上 work，它是在修复 pixel-shuffle entanglement 还是只是在 SmolVLA 的特定 action space 上 overfit？\"\n      Response 策略：M=128 passthrough control（58.0% ≈ baseline 59.2%）证明 VTR 确实在学 re-encoding 而非 action space memorization。但这个 argument 仅对 SmolVLA 成立。\n\n  - name: \"OpenVLA VTC M-Sweep (M=32/64/96)\"\n    plan_id: \"c4_ext_openvla_msweep\"\n    description: >\n      OpenVLA 上的 VTC cross-attention compressor M-sweep。所有 M 值预期失败。\n    expected_results:\n      openvla_vtc_m32_sr_pct: 0.0\n      openvla_vtc_m64_sr_pct: 0.0\n      openvla_vtc_m96_train_loss: 2.45\n      openvla_vtc_m96_sr_pct: 0.0\n      all_m_values_fail: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      M=96 已训完（final train loss 2.45, eval loss 2.66），远高于 SmolVLA VTR 的 ~0.05 train loss。这不是欠拟合——100K steps with OpenVLA 的 tokenized action space 天然产生高 cross-entropy loss。\n      M=32/M=64 的 v3/v4/v5 版本反复失败（disk full, GPU crash, training instability），即使成功训完也预期 0% SR。\n      根本原因：OpenVLA 使用 discrete tokenized actions（不是 continuous actions），VTC 的 cross-attention 将 256 个 vision tokens 压缩到 M 个 queries，但 OpenVLA 的 LLM decoder 期望完整的 256-token vision context 来做 autoregressive action token generation。压缩后的 M queries 无法提供 decoder 所需的 token-level spatial precision。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      确认 VTR/VTC 在 MLP projector + discrete action space 的组合下无效。\n      Paper 中作为 negative result 报告：VTR effectiveness = f(connector_type)，strengthens architecture-dependency narrative。\n\n  - name: \"X-VLA Cliff Threshold Localization (k=0.80/0.85, 3-seed)\"\n    plan_id: \"c1_xvla_threshold_localization\"\n    description: >\n      X-VLA 在 k=0.80 和 k=0.85 的 3-seed 精确定位 cliff。Non-monotonic pattern 已确认。\n      worst 档：cliff 是真实的，但 E5 attention pruning 证明它是 L2norm-specific artifact。\n    expected_results:\n      xvla_l2norm_k080_sr_3seed_mean: 89.0\n      xvla_l2norm_k080_sr_3seed_std: 0.72\n      xvla_l2norm_k085_sr_3seed_mean: 67.9\n      xvla_l2norm_k085_sr_3seed_std: 0.31\n      xvla_l2norm_nonmonotonic_gap_pp: 21.1\n      xvla_random_k085_sr_mean: 63.6\n      xvla_random_k080_sr_mean: 89.4\n      xvla_e5_attn_k05_sr_mean: 98.4\n      cliff_is_l2norm_specific: true\n      cliff_is_method_independent: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      X-VLA k=0.85 L2norm = 67.9%±0.31pp（3-seed，SD<1pp 确认完全 deterministic）。k=0.80 = 89.0%±0.72pp。\n      Non-monotonic gap = 21.1pp（k=0.85 < k=0.80），2-token 差异产生 21pp SR change。Random pruning 在同区间也出现 cliff（63.6% vs 89.4%），但 per-task crash pattern 不同（T4, T6 both crash across methods → architectural bottleneck）。\n      在 worst 档，这个 cliff 的意义被 E5 attention pruning 完全重新诠释：\n      - L2norm k=0.5 = 42.6% → attn_last k=0.5 = 99.2%（+56.6pp）\n      - 同样的 50 tokens，同样的 k=0.5（保留 25 tokens），attention 几乎完美而 L2norm catastrophic\n      - 因此 cliff 不是 \"BART encoder entanglement creates irreversible token dependencies\"，而是 \"L2norm 在 BART encoder 的 near-uniform norm distribution 上退化为 spatially clustered selection\"\n      - Reviewer argument：\"如果换 importance metric 就消除了 cliff，那 Axis-1 的 'token coupling' 定义有根本缺陷——关键不在 coupling 而在 importance metric。\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table H: X-VLA Cliff Zone — 3-Seed Deterministic\"\n        columns: [\"k\", \"L2norm SR(%)\", \"L2norm SD(pp)\", \"Random SR(%)\", \"Attn-Last SR(%)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0.90\", \"97.6\", \"—\", \"97.8\", \"~99\"]\n          - [\"0.85\", \"67.9\", \"0.31\", \"63.6\", \"~97\"]\n          - [\"0.80\", \"89.0\", \"0.72\", \"89.4\", \"~99\"]\n          - [\"0.70\", \"56.2\", \"—\", \"65.2\", \"99.2\"]\n          - [\"0.50\", \"42.6\", \"—\", \"70.6\", \"99.2\"]\n        notes: \"Attention pruning 完全消除 cliff 和 degradation。问题在 metric 不在 architecture。\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig X-VLA 3-method comparison: L2norm (cliff+degradation), Random (moderate degradation), Attention (near-flat). 三条 curve 在同一 plot 上，清晰展示 metric choice 的 decisive role。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cliff localization 数据本身是 solid experimental result。但在 worst 档，E5 data 完全改变其解读：\n      cliff 不是 connector architecture 的 intrinsic property，而是 L2norm importance metric 在 low-CV distribution 上的 pathological behavior。\n      Attention pruning（zero additional training）消除所有 degradation，这意味着 BART encoder 并没有 \"entangle\" tokens in a way that prevents pruning，它只是让 tokens 的 L2-norm 不再是 good importance proxy。\n      Paper 需要重新定义 Axis-1：从 \"token coupling\" 改为 \"importance metric suitability\"，或者承认 2-axis framework 是 L2norm-specific observation 而非 architecture-level insight。\n\n  - name: \"OFT CV Diagnostic (Token Importance Measurement)\"\n    plan_id: \"diagnostic_oft_cv\"\n    description: >\n      OpenVLA-OFT 的 token importance CV 测量。Expected CV≈0.219（≈Standard OpenVLA）。\n    expected_results:\n      oft_cv: 0.219\n      oft_cv_std: 0.012\n      oft_entropy: 0.667\n      openvla_standard_cv: 0.215\n      cv_delta_pp: 0.4\n      sr_eval_blocked: true\n      gpu_incompatibility: \"Blackwell SDPA requires A100+torch2.2\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      OFT CV=0.219 ≈ Standard OpenVLA CV=0.215（Δ=0.004），确认 connector（3-layer MLP）而非 action head（OFT vs standard）决定 token importance distribution。\n      Entropy 也几乎相同（0.667 vs 0.661）。这是 framework 的 positive confirmation——same connector → same CV → same predicted pruning behavior。\n      但在 worst 档，这个 data point 的价值有限：\n      (1) 无法在 LIBERO 上 eval SR（Blackwell GPU SDPA 不兼容），所以 CV 预测没有 ground truth 验证\n      (2) OFT 和 Standard OpenVLA 用相同 connector 产生相同 CV 是 trivially expected，不提供 additional discrimination power\n      (3) Reviewer 会指出：\"你们有 6 个 model 的 CV，但只有 4 个能实际 eval SR。CV 作为 predictor 的 validation set 太小。\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table I: Diagnostic Metrics — 6-Model Spectrum\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Connector\", \"CV\", \"Entropy\", \"Eval SR Available?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"π0\", \"Pure linear\", \"0.038\", \"0.959\", \"Offline only\"]\n          - [\"π0.5\", \"Pure linear (×√d)\", \"0.055\", \"—\", \"Yes (4 suites)\"]\n          - [\"X-VLA\", \"Linear + BART 12L\", \"0.151\", \"0.614\", \"Yes (4 suites)\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"3-layer MLP\", \"0.215\", \"0.661\", \"Yes (Object only)\"]\n          - [\"OFT\", \"3-layer MLP (DINOv2+SigLIP)\", \"0.219\", \"0.667\", \"No (GPU blocked)\"]\n          - [\"SmolVLA\", \"Pixel-shuffle\", \"0.314\", \"0.952\", \"Yes (4 suites)\"]\n        notes: \"6 models 有 CV，但仅 3 models 有 full cross-suite SR。OFT 和 π0 只有 diagnostic metrics。\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      OFT CV 完成了 6-model diagnostic table，但不改变任何结论。在 worst 档，这是 incrementally supportive 而非 decisive evidence。\n\n  - name: \"OFT Full Graded-Class Evaluation (4 Suites)\"\n    plan_id: \"c3_oft_graded_full\"\n    description: >\n      OpenVLA-OFT 在 4 个 LIBERO suites 上的 baseline + pruning evaluation。\n      worst 档：GPU 不兼容问题持续，无法完成 evaluation。\n    expected_results:\n      eval_blocked: true\n      blocker: \"Blackwell GPU SDPA incompatibility with OpenVLA-OFT\"\n      workaround_attempted: \"A100 rental, torch2.2 downgrade — both failed\"\n      fallback_evidence: \"CV=0.219≈OpenVLA, entropy=0.667≈0.661 — inferred graded behavior\"\n      paper_impact: \"Missing 2nd graded-class SR data point, relies on CV inference\"\n      reviewer_risk: \"Moderate — 2/3 connector classes have ≥2 SR-evaluated models, MLP class has only 1\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      OFT evaluation 在 worst 档仍然被 GPU 不兼容阻塞。Blackwell GPU 的 SDPA implementation 与 OFT checkpoint 的 torch 版本不兼容，降级 torch 或租用 A100 都不可行（timeline 限制）。\n      Paper 只能用 CV/entropy comparison 间接 argue OFT follows OpenVLA pattern。Reviewer 会注意到 MLP projector class 只有 OpenVLA 1 个 model 有 SR data，不足以 generalize。\n      CogACT（literature baseline, MLP projector, 74.8%→74.2% under 78% pruning from EfficientVLA）可以作为 external evidence，但不是 our own evaluation。\n      In worst tier, this is a clear gap but not fatal — pixel-shuffle (SmolVLA, 1 model, universal 0%) and linear (π0/π0.5, 2 models, variable) are well-characterized. MLP class has 1 internal + 1 external data point.\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Missing OFT SR data 在 worst 档是 acknowledged limitation。Reviewer concern 等级 \"moderate\"——不会 reject paper，但会要求 camera-ready 补充或更 cautious language about MLP class generalization。\n\n  - name: \"Perceiver Resampler (RoboFlamingo) — 3rd Connector Family\"\n    plan_id: \"c5_third_connector_roboflamingo\"\n    description: >\n      RoboFlamingo (Perceiver Resampler connector) 在 LIBERO 上 fine-tune + pruning。\n      worst 档：fine-tuning 产生低 baseline，且 Perceiver 不清晰地落入 2-axis taxonomy。\n    expected_results:\n      fine_tuning_baseline_sr_pct_predicted: 18.0\n      fine_tuning_difficulty: \"high — requires custom training pipeline adaptation\"\n      perceiver_cv_predicted: 0.28\n      perceiver_pruning_k09_predicted_sr_pct: 4.0\n      perceiver_pruning_k05_predicted_sr_pct: 0.0\n      taxonomy_fit: \"ambiguous — cross-attention creates partial entanglement different from both pixel-shuffle and BART\"\n      paper_inclusion: \"dropped — insufficient time and unclear taxonomy value\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      RoboFlamingo 在 worst 档面临多重困难：\n      (1) Fine-tuning infrastructure：RoboFlamingo 使用 Flamingo-style cross-attention perceiver resampler，将 variable-length vision tokens 压缩到 fixed 64 queries。这需要 custom training pipeline，previous attempts (train_c5_roboflamingo_v2) 被 killed。\n      (2) Low baseline：Perceiver Resampler 的 cross-attention 在 LIBERO manipulation tasks 上可能不如 direct projection（SmolVLA 59.2%, OpenVLA 74%），因为 LIBERO 需要 precise spatial information 而 perceiver 天然是 lossy compression。预测 baseline ~18% SR。\n      (3) Taxonomy ambiguity：Perceiver Resampler 的 cross-attention 与 BART encoder 的 self-attention 和 pixel-shuffle 的 spatial folding 都不同。它是 \"learned entanglement\" 而非 \"structural entanglement\"。CV 可能在 0.2-0.3 range，不清晰地落入现有 taxonomy。\n      (4) Timeline：距 abstract deadline 1 天，paper deadline 4 天，没有时间 debug fine-tuning pipeline + run full evaluation。\n      In worst tier, RoboFlamingo 被 dropped from paper。这减少了 paper 的 connector family 覆盖（3→2 confirmed families），但避免了 messy data 进一步复杂化已经 fragile 的 framework。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Dropping RoboFlamingo 在 worst 档是 rational choice：paper 已经有足够的 models（5 models × 4 suites）作为 empirical contribution，加入一个 low-baseline 的新 connector 只会模糊 narrative。\n      但这意味着 paper 的 connector 覆盖限于 linear/MLP/pixel-shuffle 三类，reviewer 可能指出 \"what about attention-based connectors (Perceiver, Q-Former)?\" 作为 limitation。\n\n  - name: \"VTR M-Sweep Completion (SmolVLA 3-seed × 5 M-values)\"\n    plan_id: \"c4_learned_reencoding_smolvla\"\n    description: >\n      SmolVLA VTR M-sweep 的 3-seed 完成和 MLP adapter control。\n      worst 档：数据 solid 但 M=96 dip 和 high variance 引起质疑。\n    expected_results:\n      m16_3seed_mean_sr_pct: 56.9\n      m16_3seed_std_pp: 1.3\n      m32_3seed_mean_sr_pct: 60.1\n      m32_3seed_std_pp: 1.3\n      m64_3seed_mean_sr_pct: 62.0\n      m64_3seed_std_pp: 2.3\n      m96_3seed_mean_sr_pct: 54.5\n      m96_3seed_std_pp: 3.2\n      m128_3seed_mean_sr_pct: 58.0\n      m128_3seed_std_pp: 3.5\n      mlp_adapter_m32_3seed_mean_sr_pct: 63.4\n      mlp_adapter_m32_3seed_std_pp: 2.6\n      vtc_vs_mlp_pvalue: 0.15\n      m64_vs_m96_pvalue: 0.034\n      baseline_sr_pct: 59.2\n      m_curve_flat_within_3pp: true\n      m96_dip_significant: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      VTR M-sweep 数据 intrinsically solid：M=16(56.9%) 到 M=128(58.0%) 都在 baseline 59.2% 的 ±5pp 内，证明 near-lossless compression at any ratio。MLP adapter control（63.4%）与 VTC（60.1%）无显著差异（p=0.15），确认 architecture independence。\n      但 worst 档关注两个 weakness：\n      (1) M=96 dip（54.5%, p=0.034 vs M=64=62.0%）虽然在 Bonferroni correction 后 marginally significant，但 3.2pp std 是所有 M 值中最高的。这暗示 training instability——某些 seed/M 组合在 training dynamics 中进入 suboptimal basin。\n      (2) M=128 passthrough 的 3.5pp std 也高，且 seed43=54.0% 是 outlier（其他两个 seed 59.8/60.2%）。如果 passthrough control 本身有 6pp variance，\"near-lossless\" 的声称需要 caveat。\n      In worst tier, VTR 仍然是 valid method（0%→~59% recovery），但 training stability concern 使其从 \"recommended practice\" 降级为 \"promising but needs further investigation\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table J: VTR M-Sweep 3-Seed Results\"\n        columns: [\"M\", \"Compression(%)\", \"Mean SR(%)\", \"Std(pp)\", \"Individual Seeds\", \"vs Baseline\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"16\", \"87.5\", \"56.9\", \"1.3\", \"55.8/58.4/56.5\", \"-2.3pp\"]\n          - [\"32\", \"75.0\", \"60.1\", \"1.3\", \"61.6/59.2/59.6\", \"+0.9pp\"]\n          - [\"64\", \"50.0\", \"62.0\", \"2.3\", \"61.6/60.0/64.4\", \"+2.8pp\"]\n          - [\"96\", \"25.0\", \"54.5\", \"3.2\", \"52.6/58.2/52.8\", \"-4.7pp\"]\n          - [\"128\", \"0.0\", \"58.0\", \"3.5\", \"59.8/54.0/60.2\", \"-1.2pp\"]\n          - [\"MLP-32\", \"75.0\", \"63.4\", \"2.6\", \"65.2/64.6/60.4\", \"+4.2pp\"]\n        notes: \"M=96 dip p=0.034。M=128 seed43=54.0 outlier。Flat M-curve 成立但 variance 在高 M 处增大。\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig M-curve with 3-seed error bars and baseline band (59.2%±3pp shaded). M=96 dip 和 M=128 variance clearly visible。\"\n    analysis: >\n      VTR 在 worst 档仍是 paper 的 positive contribution：hard pruning 0% → VTR ~59% ≈ baseline 是 dramatic recovery。\n      但 M=96 dip 和 high-M variance 需要 honest reporting。建议 paper 用 M=32 或 M=64 作为 recommended setting（stable seeds, good compression ratio），将 M=96 dip 作为 \"open question: why does M=96 underperform?\" 放入 discussion。\n      Reviewer concern level: low-moderate. VTR 的 core claim（recovery from 0% to baseline）is robust. M=96 是 interesting anomaly 但不 undermine main contribution。\n\n  - name: \"Consolidated Cross-Suite Framework Accuracy Assessment\"\n    plan_id: \"c6_libero_suite_expansion\"\n    description: >\n      综合所有 cross-suite 数据的 framework 准确率评估。\n      worst 档：framework accuracy ~62%，不足以支撑 \"principled framework\" 定位。\n    expected_results:\n      framework_predictions_total: 20\n      framework_predictions_correct: 12\n      framework_accuracy_pct: 62\n      claims_surviving_review: 2.5\n      surviving_claims: \"C2 (pixel-shuffle entanglement), C4 (VTR case study), partial C3b (MLP graded)\"\n      failed_claims: \"C1 (2-axis framework as principled theory), C5 (CV universal predictor)\"\n      reframed_claims: \"C1→empirical observation catalog, C5→within-suite heuristic\"\n      paper_contribution_type: \"empirical study with surprising findings\"\n      corl_submission_viable: true\n      corl_acceptance_probability_pct: 45\n    result_rationale: >\n      Framework accuracy 计算方法：\n      - SmolVLA × 4 suites: 预测 \"catastrophic at k=0.95\" → 实际 all suites ≤0.1% → 4/4 correct\n      - X-VLA × 4 suites: 预测 \"entangling, task-dependent collapse\" → Object OK (97.6%), Goal 70.2% (partial collapse), Spatial 78.8% (moderate), Long 27.5% (collapse) → 3/4 correct（Object 不 collapse，与预测不符）\n      - π0.5 × 4 suites: 预测 \"independent, immune to task complexity\" → Object random k=0.9=9%（NOT immune!），但 L2norm=98.2% → method-dependent → 1/4 correct（框架不区分 method）\n      - OpenVLA × 4 suites: 预测 \"graded, L2norm preferred\" → Object L2norm>random (+1.8pp ✓), Goal random>L2norm (+8.8pp ✗) → 2/4 correct\n      - π0 × offline: 预测 \"immune\" → k=0.1 improves → 1/1 correct\n      Total: 4+3+1+2+1 = 11/17 = 65%（≈62% with margin of error）\n\n      Claims survival analysis:\n      - C1 (2-axis framework): FAILS as theory → survives as \"descriptive taxonomy for L2norm pruning on Object suite\"\n      - C2 (pixel-shuffle entanglement): SURVIVES — universal 0% across all suites/methods/k is unambiguous\n      - C3a (linear proj depends on pipeline): Partially survives — π0 immune, π0.5 method-dependent, X-VLA cliff\n      - C3b (MLP graded): Survives on Object — graded curve confirmed\n      - C4 (VTR): Survives as SmolVLA case study — 0%→59% recovery\n      - C5 (CV predicts strategy): FAILS as universal law → survives as \"within-Object-suite heuristic\"\n\n      2.5 claims survive: C2, C4, half of C3b.\n\n      CoRL viability: paper 作为 \"comprehensive empirical study\" 仍然 viable（5 models × 4 suites × 3 methods 是任何 VLA pruning 工作中最大规模的 comparison）。Acceptance probability ~45%——足够好的 empirical contribution 但缺少 unified theory 会让某些 reviewers 觉得 \"incremental\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table K: Framework Prediction Accuracy by Model\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Connector Class\", \"Framework Prediction\", \"Object\", \"Spatial\", \"Goal\", \"Long\", \"Accuracy\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"SmolVLA\", \"Pixel-shuffle\", \"Catastrophic all suites\", \"✓\", \"✓\", \"✓\", \"✓\", \"4/4\"]\n          - [\"X-VLA\", \"BART encoder\", \"Task-dependent collapse\", \"✗(no collapse)\", \"✓\", \"✓\", \"✓\", \"3/4\"]\n          - [\"π0.5\", \"Linear proj\", \"Immune to task complexity\", \"✗(random cliff)\", \"✗\", \"✗\", \"✗\", \"1/4\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"MLP\", \"Graded, L2norm preferred\", \"✓\", \"~\", \"✗(random preferred)\", \"~\", \"2/4\"]\n          - [\"π0\", \"Linear proj\", \"Immune\", \"✓(offline)\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\", \"1/1\"]\n        notes: \"Total 11/17 ≈ 65%。π0.5 是 framework 最大 failure point。\"\n      - title: \"Table L: Claim Survival Assessment\"\n        columns: [\"Claim\", \"Original Status\", \"Worst-Tier Status\", \"Surviving Evidence\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"C1: 2-Axis Framework\", \"Primary contribution\", \"Fails as theory\", \"Descriptive taxonomy for L2norm-Object only\"]\n          - [\"C2: Pixel-Shuffle Entanglement\", \"Strong\", \"Survives\", \"Universal 0% across 4 suites × 2 methods\"]\n          - [\"C3: Connector-Specific Patterns\", \"Strong\", \"Partial survival\", \"MLP graded confirmed; linear 'immune' falsified\"]\n          - [\"C4: VTR Recovery\", \"Strong\", \"Survives as case study\", \"0%→59% on SmolVLA; fails on OpenVLA\"]\n          - [\"C5: CV Scaling Law\", \"Novel contribution\", \"Fails as universal\", \"Within-Object heuristic only; cross-suite |ρ|≈0.45\"]\n        notes: \"2-3 claims survive review intact. Paper viable as empirical study, not as theory paper.\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig framework accuracy heatmap: 5 models × 4 suites grid, color = (prediction correct / partially correct / wrong). Visual impact: scattered errors, no clean pattern.\"\n      - \"Fig revised paper narrative flow: from 'discover governing principle' to 'provide systematic benchmark + catalog surprising findings'.\"\n    analysis: >\n      在 worst 档，paper 的 identity 发生根本转变：\n      FROM: \"We discover a principled 2-axis framework governing VLA token compressibility\"\n      TO: \"We provide the first systematic study of token pruning across VLA architectures, revealing that pruning behavior is an irreducible function of (connector, method, k, task), not reducible to simple architectural rules\"\n\n      Key novel findings that survive independently of the framework:\n      (1) Pixel-shuffle entanglement is real and irreversible — this is a genuine architectural insight\n      (2) Importance metric selection matters more than connector architecture — supported by E5 attention data + π0.5 method divergence\n      (3) L2norm is actively harmful on low-CV models — 36pp gap on π0.5, 28pp on X-VLA at k=0.5 Object\n      (4) VTR achieves near-lossless compression for pixel-shuffle — 0%→59% at any M ratio\n\n      These 4 findings are individually publishable observations that together constitute a substantial empirical contribution for CoRL, even without a unified theory. Title: \"A Systematic Study of Token Pruning Strategies Across VLA Architectures.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1043,"cache_read_input_tokens":127511,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1043},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0a5ab60b-18ac-4b1d-b58b-ab75725b2ce1","uuid":"a42a0eb0-8aef-4566-807a-c81908a72ba2"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":603360,"duration_api_ms":606059,"num_turns":7,"result":"Now I have the full experiment plan. Let me cross-reference with the existing registry data to generate worst-tier predictions.\n\n```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  核心 reframe：从 'principled 2-axis framework' 转为 'comprehensive empirical study of VLA token pruning across architectures and tasks'。\n  π0.5 cross-suite 数据摧毁了两轴独立性假设——random k=0.9 在 Object=9% vs Goal=62.2%，同一 token-independent connector 跨 suite 差异达 53pp。\n  E5 attention pruning 数据（X-VLA k=0.5 attn_last=99.2% vs L2norm=42.6%）证明 'entanglement' 不是 connector 的固有属性，而是 importance metric 选择的 artifact。\n  CV scaling law 仅在 Object suite 内部成立（Spearman ρ=-1.0），跨 suite 后 Long-horizon 出现反转（π0.5 L2norm > random），平均 |ρ|≈0.45。\n  VTR 确认为 SmolVLA-specific 方案（OpenVLA VTC-only 全部失败），且 M=96 dip (p=0.034) 暗示训练不稳定。\n  Title 改为 'A Systematic Study of Token Pruning Strategies Across VLA Architectures'。\n  仍然 submit CoRL，因为 5 models × 4 suites × systematic comparison 是 substantial empirical contribution。\n  Claims 缩减为：(1) pixel-shuffle entanglement 是真实的架构属性（C2 survives），(2) importance metric 选择 > connector architecture（new empirical finding），(3) VTR 在 pixel-shuffle 上实现 near-lossless compression（C4 survives as case study）。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  - name: \"Cross-Suite Expansion: π0.5 + X-VLA + OpenVLA + SmolVLA × 4 Suites\"\n    plan_id: \"c6_libero_suite_expansion\"\n    description: >\n      将所有 5 models 的 pruning 实验从 Object 扩展到 Spatial/Goal/Long。\n      核心目的：验证 2-axis framework 的 cross-suite 一致性。\n      实际结果：framework 在 Object suite 上准确，但 cross-suite 后出现系统性偏差。\n    expected_results:\n      pi05_random_k09_object_sr_pct: 9.3\n      pi05_random_k09_goal_sr_pct: 62.2\n      pi05_random_k09_spatial_sr_pct: 54.0\n      pi05_random_k09_long_sr_pct: 31.4\n      pi05_random_k09_cross_suite_range_pp: 52.9\n      pi05_l2norm_k09_object_sr_pct: 98.2\n      pi05_l2norm_k09_goal_sr_pct: 89.6\n      pi05_l2norm_k09_spatial_sr_pct: 95.3\n      pi05_l2norm_k09_long_sr_pct: 80.0\n      pi05_l2norm_k09_cross_suite_range_pp: 18.2\n      xvla_l2norm_k09_object_sr_pct: 97.6\n      xvla_l2norm_k09_goal_sr_pct: 70.2\n      xvla_l2norm_k09_spatial_sr_pct: 78.8\n      xvla_l2norm_k09_long_sr_pct: 27.5\n      xvla_l2norm_k095_long_sr_pct: 47.0\n      smolvla_k095_all_suites_sr_pct: \"<0.1 (all 4 suites)\"\n      cv_strategy_spearman_object: -1.0\n      cv_strategy_spearman_goal: -0.5\n      cv_strategy_spearman_long: 0.5\n      cv_strategy_abs_spearman_mean: 0.45\n      delta_R_L2_k05_pi05_object_pp: 36.0\n      delta_R_L2_k05_pi05_goal_pp: 13.8\n      delta_R_L2_k05_pi05_long_pp: -4.6\n      delta_R_L2_k05_xvla_object_pp: 28.0\n      delta_R_L2_k05_xvla_goal_pp: 8.5\n      delta_R_L2_k05_xvla_long_pp: 17.0\n      delta_R_L2_k05_openvla_object_pp: -1.8\n      delta_R_L2_k05_openvla_goal_pp: 8.8\n      framework_accuracy_pct: 62\n      axis2_amplification_entangling_minus_independent_pp: 11.4\n      e5_xvla_attn_last_k05_object_sr_pct: 99.2\n      e5_xvla_attn_last_k05_goal_sr_pct: 98.2\n      e5_xvla_attn_last_k05_spatial_sr_pct: 88.8\n      e5_xvla_attn_last_k05_long_sr_pct: 90.2\n      e5_xvla_attn_mean_k05_long_sr_pct: 94.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      π0.5 random k=0.9 在 Object 上出现 catastrophic cliff（9.3%），但在 Goal 上仅下降至 62.2%——同一 linear projection connector、同一 random method、同一 k，仅 task distribution 不同就产生 53pp 差异。这直接破坏 \"token-independent connector 不受 task complexity 影响\" 的核心假设。\n      机制：Object suite 需要 precise object identity discrimination（visually similar condiments），random 在 cliff zone 摧毁 concentrated discriminative features；Goal suite 的 task 由 language instruction 区分，vision tokens 冗余度更高，random 破坏的影响小。\n      L2norm 在相同 k=0.9 的 cross-suite range 仅 18.2pp（vs random 53pp），证明 cross-suite sensitivity 是 METHOD-dependent 而非 connector-dependent。\n      E5 attention pruning 数据更具破坏性：X-VLA k=0.5 attn_last=99.2%（Object）、98.2%（Goal），vs L2norm=42.6%/59%。这意味着 X-VLA 的 \"entanglement\" 问题完全可以通过更换 importance metric 解决，BART encoder 产生的不是 \"irreversible entanglement\" 而是 \"norm-unfriendly importance distribution\"。\n      CV scaling law 在 Object 内仍然成立（Spearman -1.0），但 Long-horizon 出现反转（π0.5 L2norm > random，Δ=-4.6pp），导致 cross-suite 平均 |ρ|≈0.45，远低于 paper 声称的 \"universal predictor\" 所需的 >0.8。\n      OpenVLA 在 Goal 上也出现 method preference reversal（random > L2norm +8.8pp），而 Object 上 L2norm > random（+1.8pp）。同一 CV=0.215 的 model，跨 suite 后 method preference 反转。\n      Framework 在 20 个 model×suite 预测中仅正确约 12 个（62%），达不到 \"principled framework\" 标准。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table A: Cross-Suite Δ(Random-L2norm) at k=0.5 — CV Scaling Law Breakdown\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"CV\", \"Object Δ(pp)\", \"Spatial Δ(pp)\", \"Goal Δ(pp)\", \"Long Δ(pp)\", \"Range(pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"π0.5\", \"0.055\", \"+36.0\", \"+16.0\", \"+13.8\", \"-4.6\", \"40.6\"]\n          - [\"X-VLA\", \"0.151\", \"+28.0\", \"+12.6\", \"+8.5\", \"+17.0\", \"19.5\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"0.215\", \"-1.8\", \"~+5\", \"+8.8\", \"~+3\", \"~10.6\"]\n        notes: \"Object suite 上 monotonic（ρ=-1.0），Long suite 上 π0.5 reversal 破坏 monotonicity。Cross-suite mean |ρ|≈0.45。\"\n      - title: \"Table B: π0.5 Random k=0.9 Cross-Suite — Token-Independent ≠ Task-Independent\"\n        columns: [\"Suite\", \"Baseline(%)\", \"Random k=0.9(%)\", \"Δ from baseline(pp)\", \"L2norm k=0.9(%)\", \"Method gap(pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Object\", \"98.2\", \"9.3\", \"-88.9\", \"98.2\", \"-88.9\"]\n          - [\"Spatial\", \"97.2\", \"54.0\", \"-43.2\", \"95.3\", \"-41.3\"]\n          - [\"Goal\", \"96.4\", \"62.2\", \"-34.2\", \"89.6\", \"-27.4\"]\n          - [\"Long\", \"92.8\", \"31.4\", \"-61.4\", \"80.0\", \"-12.8\"]\n        notes: \"Cross-suite range 53pp for random vs 18pp for L2norm。Task sensitivity 是 method-specific，非 architecture-level property。\"\n      - title: \"Table C: E5 Attention Pruning Demolishes Entanglement Narrative (X-VLA k=0.5)\"\n        columns: [\"Suite\", \"L2norm(%)\", \"Random(%)\", \"Attn-Last(%)\", \"Attn-Mean(%)\", \"Best Attn vs L2norm(pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Object\", \"42.6\", \"70.6\", \"99.2\", \"98.4\", \"+56.6\"]\n          - [\"Spatial\", \"58.8\", \"71.4\", \"88.8\", \"91.6\", \"+32.8\"]\n          - [\"Goal\", \"59.0\", \"67.2\", \"98.2\", \"97.4\", \"+38.4\"]\n          - [\"Long\", \"44.6\", \"61.6\", \"90.2\", \"94.0\", \"+49.4\"]\n        notes: \"Attention pruning 在所有 4 suites 上实现 88-99% SR at k=0.5。问题不在 connector entanglement，在 importance metric。\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig cross-suite heatmap: 5 models × 4 suites × 2 methods (L2norm/random) at k=0.5/k=0.9, 颜色编码 SR。清晰展示 framework 预测（虚线框）vs 实际结果的 mismatch areas。\"\n      - \"Fig CV vs Δ(R-L2) scatter: 4 panels (one per suite), 每个 panel 3 个点 (π0.5/X-VLA/OpenVLA)，展示 scaling law 在 Object 上线性但在 Long 上崩溃。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cross-suite 数据系统性地破坏 2-axis framework 的两个核心预测：\n      (1) Axis-1 独立性：token-independent connectors should be immune to task complexity → π0.5 random k=0.9 Object=9% vs Goal=62% 证伪（53pp gap）。\n      (2) CV universal predictor：CV 应在所有 suite 上预测 method preference → Long-horizon 上 π0.5 出现 reversal（L2norm > random），OpenVLA 在 Goal 上也 reversal。\n      E5 attention pruning 数据进一步瓦解 Axis-1 定义：X-VLA（\"entangling\"）在 attention pruning 下表现如同 \"independent\" connector。Axis-1 的区分不在 \"token coupling\" 而在 \"susceptibility to norm-based importance bias\"。\n      Reframe：论文不能声称发现了 governing principle，而应定位为 \"comprehensive empirical study revealing that importance metric selection matters more than connector architecture\"。\n\n  - name: \"π0.5 Token-Independent Confirmation (4B, Linear Proj)\"\n    plan_id: \"c1_pi05_immune_confirmation\"\n    description: >\n      π0.5 作为 2nd token-independent data point，验证 CV=0.055 的 linear projection 在所有 suite 上的 pruning 行为。\n      worst 档：π0.5 数据揭示 \"immune class\" 不存在——random pruning 在 cliff zone (k=0.85-0.925) 产生 catastrophic collapse，且行为极度 task-dependent。\n    expected_results:\n      pi05_cv: 0.055\n      pi05_baseline_object_sr_pct: 98.2\n      pi05_baseline_spatial_sr_pct: 97.2\n      pi05_baseline_goal_sr_pct: 96.4\n      pi05_baseline_long_sr_pct: 92.8\n      pi05_random_k095_object_sr_pct: 71.1\n      pi05_random_k0925_object_sr_pct: 27.6\n      pi05_random_k09_object_sr_pct: 10.8\n      pi05_random_k085_object_sr_pct: 5.0\n      pi05_random_k07_object_sr_pct: 75.5\n      pi05_random_k05_object_sr_pct: 69.4\n      pi05_l2norm_k09_object_sr_pct: 98.2\n      pi05_l2norm_k085_object_sr_pct: 98.0\n      pi05_l2norm_k05_object_sr_pct: 33.4\n      pi05_l2norm_k03_object_sr_pct: 51.0\n      pi05_random_cliff_depth_pp: 66.1\n      pi05_l2norm_v_shape_depth_pp: 17.6\n      pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k05_cross_suite_avg_pp: 15.3\n      pi05_attention_k07_object_sr_pct: 0.6\n      pi05_attention_k05_object_sr_pct: 37.8\n      pi05_attention_k095_object_sr_pct: 98.4\n    result_rationale: >\n      π0.5（CV=0.055）本应是 \"immune\" class 的完美验证，但数据揭示了截然不同的图景：\n      (1) Random-specific cliff：k=0.95→71.1% → k=0.925→27.6% → k=0.9→10.8% → k=0.85→5.0%，在 10% keep ratio 变化范围内产生 66pp collapse。这个 cliff 是 random-specific 的——L2norm 在同区间保持 98.0-99.2% 的 plateau。\n      (2) Fixed-mask experiment 排除了 temporal inconsistency（T0=12% = per-call 12%），证明 cliff 是 spatial coverage 的 structural failure。\n      (3) V-shape non-monotonicity：L2norm 在 k=0.5 出现 valley（33.4%），k=0.7=55.0% 和 k=0.3=51.0% 都更高。Token position visualization 确认 k=0.5 恰好是 spatial clustering 最严重的点（1 cluster, 78% coverage）。\n      (4) Cross-suite 数据摧毁 \"immune\" 标签：random k=0.9 在 Object=9% 但 Goal=62.2%（+53pp），Spatial=54%，Long=31.4%。Object 的 concentrated critical features（visually similar condiments）在 cliff zone 极度脆弱，而 Goal 的 language-disambiguated tasks 对 random token loss 更 robust。\n      (5) Attention pruning 不解决问题：k=0.7 attn=0.6%（比 random 的 75.5% 差 75pp），k=0.5 attn=37.8%（与 L2norm 33.4% 持平）。π0.5 的 attention map 不提供有效 importance signal。\n      In worst tier, π0.5 从 \"immune class exemplar\" 降级为 \"case study demonstrating that pruning behavior is an irreducible function of method × k × task, not a simple connector property\"。Cross-suite average Δ(R-L2) at k=0.5 = (+36+16+13.8-4.6)/4 = 15.3pp，远低于 Object-only 的 36pp。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table D: π0.5 Random Cliff Zone (Object Suite)\"\n        columns: [\"k\", \"Tokens kept\", \"Random SR(%)\", \"L2norm SR(%)\", \"Δ(L2-R)(pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0.95\", \"730\", \"71.1\", \"98.2\", \"+27.1\"]\n          - [\"0.925\", \"710\", \"27.6\", \"99.2\", \"+71.6\"]\n          - [\"0.90\", \"691\", \"10.8\", \"98.2\", \"+87.4\"]\n          - [\"0.85\", \"653\", \"5.0\", \"98.0\", \"+93.0\"]\n          - [\"0.70\", \"538\", \"75.5\", \"55.0\", \"-20.5\"]\n          - [\"0.50\", \"384\", \"69.4\", \"33.4\", \"-36.0\"]\n          - [\"0.30\", \"230\", \"36.4\", \"51.0\", \"+14.6\"]\n        notes: \"方法偏好在 k=0.7 附近反转。Cliff zone (k=0.85-0.925) L2norm 完胜；aggressive zone (k=0.5-0.7) random 完胜。\"\n      - title: \"Table E: π0.5 Cross-Suite Random k=0.9 — 'Immune' Class Falsified\"\n        columns: [\"Suite\", \"Baseline(%)\", \"Random k=0.9(%)\", \"L2norm k=0.9(%)\", \"Δ from baseline (random, pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Object\", \"98.2\", \"9.3\", \"98.2\", \"-88.9\"]\n          - [\"Spatial\", \"97.2\", \"54.0\", \"95.3\", \"-43.2\"]\n          - [\"Goal\", \"96.4\", \"62.2\", \"89.6\", \"-34.2\"]\n          - [\"Long\", \"92.8\", \"31.4\", \"80.0\", \"-61.4\"]\n        notes: \"同一 model/method/k，cross-suite range=53pp。Framework 预测 token-independent 应 <5pp variation。\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig π0.5 dual-method pruning curve: x=k, y=SR, two lines (random/L2norm), Object suite。突出 random cliff zone 和 L2norm V-shape valley。\"\n      - \"Fig π0.5 4-suite comparison: 4 panels, 每 panel 一个 suite, random+L2norm curves。展示 cross-suite behavior divergence。\"\n    analysis: >\n      π0.5 数据是 worst 档的 smoking gun：CV=0.055 的 pure linear projection 不 \"immune\"，只是 L2norm 恰好在 cliff zone 有效。\n      换用 random pruning，即出现 catastrophic cliff。换 suite（Goal/Long），random 的 cliff 消失但 L2norm 的 advantage 也缩小。\n      这意味着 \"compressibility\" 不是 connector 的 intrinsic property，而是 (connector, method, k, task) 四元组的 emergent property。\n      2-axis framework 的简化——将其压缩为 (connector, task) 二维——在 worst 档数据下失效。\n      Paper 需要 reframe：不是 \"connector determines compressibility\"，而是 \"we provide the first comprehensive map of the 4D pruning landscape across VLA architectures\"。\n\n  - name: \"VTR Cross-Suite Generalization (SmolVLA M=32 on Spatial/Goal/Long)\"\n    plan_id: \"c6_libero_suite_vtr\"\n    description: >\n      SmolVLA VTR M=32 在 Spatial/Goal/Long suites 上的压缩性能验证。\n      worst 档：VTR cross-suite recovery 衰减，且 VTR 训练在非 Object suite 上有不稳定性。\n    expected_results:\n      vtr_m32_object_sr_pct: 60.1\n      vtr_m32_spatial_sr_pct: 53.2\n      vtr_m32_goal_sr_pct: 56.4\n      vtr_m32_long_sr_pct_predicted: 48.0\n      smolvla_baseline_object_sr_pct: 59.2\n      smolvla_baseline_spatial_sr_pct: 44.6\n      smolvla_baseline_goal_sr_pct: 60.8\n      smolvla_baseline_long_sr_pct: 36.6\n      vtr_recovery_ratio_object: 1.015\n      vtr_recovery_ratio_spatial: 1.193\n      vtr_recovery_ratio_goal: 0.928\n      vtr_recovery_ratio_long_predicted: 0.874\n      vtr_recovery_ratio_mean: 0.95\n      vtr_m96_dip_p_value: 0.034\n      vtr_m96_dip_confirmed: true\n      hard_pruning_k05_all_suites_sr_pct: 0.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      VTR M=32 在 Object 上实现 near-lossless compression（60.1% vs baseline 59.2%），Spatial 上甚至超过 baseline（53.2% vs 44.6%，可能因为 VTR 训练 regularization 效应）。\n      但 Goal suite recovery ratio = 56.4/60.8 = 0.928，低于 Object。预测 Long-horizon（未测）recovery ratio 进一步下降至 ~0.87：Long tasks 需要 multi-step reasoning，VTR 的 cross-attention 可能无法完全保留 temporal action sequence 所需的 spatial information chain。\n      M=96 dip（p=0.034 vs M=64）在 worst 档被确认为 training instability（非 statistical fluke），因为 M=96 的 3-seed std=3.2pp 是所有 M 值中最高的。这暗示 VTR 的 flat M-curve 可能是 M=16-64 的幸运区间，M=96 暴露了 cross-attention query 数量与 pixel-shuffle token structure 之间的 resonance 问题。\n      VTR 仍然是 valid contribution（从 0% hard pruning 恢复到 ~baseline），但 worst 档将其定位为 \"SmolVLA-specific case study\" 而非 \"general method\"，因为：\n      (1) cross-suite recovery 有衰减（Goal 0.93, Long predicted 0.87），\n      (2) M=96 dip 暗示 training sensitivity，\n      (3) OpenVLA VTR 完全失败（下条）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table F: VTR M=32 Cross-Suite Recovery (SmolVLA)\"\n        columns: [\"Suite\", \"Hard Prune k=0.5(%)\", \"VTR M=32(%)\", \"Baseline(%)\", \"Recovery Ratio\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Object\", \"0.0\", \"60.1\", \"59.2\", \"1.015\"]\n          - [\"Spatial\", \"0.6\", \"53.2\", \"44.6\", \"1.193\"]\n          - [\"Goal\", \"0.0\", \"56.4\", \"60.8\", \"0.928\"]\n          - [\"Long (pred)\", \"0.0\", \"~48\", \"36.6\", \"~0.87\"]\n        notes: \"Recovery ratio 从 Object(1.0) 下降到 Long(0.87)。VTR 在 complex tasks 上 recovery 衰减 ~13%。\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig VTR M-curve with error bars: x=M, y=SR, 3-seed error bars。M=96 dip 突出标注 p=0.034。\"\n      - \"Fig VTR cross-suite bar chart: 4 suites × (hard prune / VTR M=32 / baseline)，展示 recovery gap 在 Long 上最大。\"\n    analysis: >\n      VTR 从 \"universal compression method\" 降级为 \"effective recovery tool for pixel-shuffle connectors, with decreasing efficacy on complex tasks\"。\n      M=96 dip 的 statistical significance (p=0.034) 不足以证明 systematic failure（n=3 power ~0.2），但足以引起 reviewer 对 training stability 的质疑。\n      Cross-suite recovery 衰减是合理的：VTR 在 Object suite 上训练，cross-suite 是 zero-shot transfer。Long-horizon tasks 的 action sequence 依赖 precise temporal-spatial correspondence，VTR 的 cross-attention bottleneck 可能丢失这些 long-range dependencies。\n      Paper 策略：VTR 作为 §4.7 的 case study 保留，但移除 \"universal compression\" 措辞，改为 \"recovers pixel-shuffle cliff-edge to near-baseline on trained distribution, with ~13% degradation on out-of-distribution complex tasks\"。\n\n  - name: \"VTR Universality Test: OpenVLA MLP Projector (M=128/32/64)\"\n    plan_id: \"c4_ext_method_universality_openvla\"\n    description: >\n      VTR 在 OpenVLA（MLP projector）上的泛化性测试。M=128 full VTR 已失败（0% SR），VTC-only M=32/M=64 作为 fallback。\n    expected_results:\n      openvla_vtr_m128_sr_pct: 0.0\n      openvla_vtconly_m32_sr_pct_predicted: 3.0\n      openvla_vtconly_m64_sr_pct_predicted: 5.0\n      openvla_vtconly_m96_sr_pct_predicted: 2.0\n      openvla_baseline_sr_pct: 74.0\n      overfitting_confirmed: true\n      failure_mode: \"model outputs identical action every timestep\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      M=128 VTR 在 20K steps 后 0% SR（model 对所有 observation 输出相同 action）确认 severe overfitting。\n      VTC-only M=32/M=64 预测同样失败（<5% SR），因为根本原因不在 VTR architecture 而在 MLP projector tokens 的特性：\n      (1) MLP projector tokens 已经是 individually meaningful 的（CV=0.215, 有 gradient differentiation），VTR 的 cross-attention 无法提供额外信息，反而引入 information bottleneck。\n      (2) OpenVLA 的 256 tokens × 7B parameters 的 scale 与 SmolVLA 的 128 tokens × 450M parameters 完全不同——VTR 的 ~22M params 对 7B model 来说是 rounding error，无法学到有意义的 re-encoding。\n      (3) M=96/M=64/M=32 的 training loss 持续下降但 eval SR 不恢复，典型的 action space overfitting pattern。\n      在 worst 档，这确认 VTR 是 pixel-shuffle-specific method。Paper 中 VTR 需要 reframe：不是 \"universal compression tool\" 而是 \"architecture-specific recovery mechanism that works because pixel-shuffle tokens need re-entangling, while MLP tokens are already independent and don't benefit from cross-attention re-encoding\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table G: VTR on OpenVLA — Universal Failure\"\n        columns: [\"Config\", \"M\", \"Params(M)\", \"Steps\", \"Train Loss\", \"SR(%)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Full VTR\", \"128\", \"22.2\", \"20K\", \"converged\", \"0.0\"]\n          - [\"VTC-only\", \"32\", \"22.2\", \"100K\", \"converged\", \"~3\"]\n          - [\"VTC-only\", \"64\", \"22.2\", \"100K\", \"converged\", \"~5\"]\n          - [\"VTC-only\", \"96\", \"22.2\", \"100K\", \"converged\", \"~2\"]\n          - [\"LoRA baseline\", \"—\", \"883\", \"100K\", \"0.065\", \"0.0\"]\n        notes: \"所有 VTR configs 失败。Train loss 收敛但 SR ≈0。Failure mode: identical action output。\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig overfitting diagnostic: training loss curve (converging) + eval SR curve (flat at 0%), 展示 train/eval disconnect。\"\n    analysis: >\n      VTR universality 完全失败。这不是 hyperparameter tuning 问题——M=128/96/64/32 全部 <5% SR，且 LoRA fine-tuning 也产生 0% SR（libero_lora_baseline），说明 OpenVLA 的 fine-tuning 本身就 fragile。\n      Reviewer 会问：\"如果 VTR 只在 SmolVLA 上 work，它是在修复 pixel-shuffle entanglement 还是只是在 SmolVLA 的特定 action space 上 overfit？\"\n      Response 策略：M=128 passthrough control（58.0% ≈ baseline 59.2%）证明 VTR 确实在学 re-encoding 而非 action space memorization。但这个 argument 仅对 SmolVLA 成立。\n\n  - name: \"OpenVLA VTC M-Sweep (M=32/64/96)\"\n    plan_id: \"c4_ext_openvla_msweep\"\n    description: >\n      OpenVLA 上的 VTC cross-attention compressor M-sweep。所有 M 值预期失败。\n    expected_results:\n      openvla_vtc_m32_sr_pct: 0.0\n      openvla_vtc_m64_sr_pct: 0.0\n      openvla_vtc_m96_train_loss: 2.45\n      openvla_vtc_m96_sr_pct: 0.0\n      all_m_values_fail: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      M=96 已训完（final train loss 2.45, eval loss 2.66），远高于 SmolVLA VTR 的 ~0.05 train loss。这不是欠拟合——100K steps with OpenVLA 的 tokenized action space 天然产生高 cross-entropy loss。\n      M=32/M=64 的 v3/v4/v5 版本反复失败（disk full, GPU crash, training instability），即使成功训完也预期 0% SR。\n      根本原因：OpenVLA 使用 discrete tokenized actions（不是 continuous actions），VTC 的 cross-attention 将 256 个 vision tokens 压缩到 M 个 queries，但 OpenVLA 的 LLM decoder 期望完整的 256-token vision context 来做 autoregressive action token generation。压缩后的 M queries 无法提供 decoder 所需的 token-level spatial precision。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      确认 VTR/VTC 在 MLP projector + discrete action space 的组合下无效。\n      Paper 中作为 negative result 报告：VTR effectiveness = f(connector_type)，strengthens architecture-dependency narrative。\n\n  - name: \"X-VLA Cliff Threshold Localization (k=0.80/0.85, 3-seed)\"\n    plan_id: \"c1_xvla_threshold_localization\"\n    description: >\n      X-VLA 在 k=0.80 和 k=0.85 的 3-seed 精确定位 cliff。Non-monotonic pattern 已确认。\n      worst 档：cliff 是真实的，但 E5 attention pruning 证明它是 L2norm-specific artifact。\n    expected_results:\n      xvla_l2norm_k080_sr_3seed_mean: 89.0\n      xvla_l2norm_k080_sr_3seed_std: 0.72\n      xvla_l2norm_k085_sr_3seed_mean: 67.9\n      xvla_l2norm_k085_sr_3seed_std: 0.31\n      xvla_l2norm_nonmonotonic_gap_pp: 21.1\n      xvla_random_k085_sr_mean: 63.6\n      xvla_random_k080_sr_mean: 89.4\n      xvla_e5_attn_k05_sr_mean: 98.4\n      cliff_is_l2norm_specific: true\n      cliff_is_method_independent: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      X-VLA k=0.85 L2norm = 67.9%±0.31pp（3-seed，SD<1pp 确认完全 deterministic）。k=0.80 = 89.0%±0.72pp。\n      Non-monotonic gap = 21.1pp（k=0.85 < k=0.80），2-token 差异产生 21pp SR change。Random pruning 在同区间也出现 cliff（63.6% vs 89.4%），但 per-task crash pattern 不同（T4, T6 both crash across methods → architectural bottleneck）。\n      在 worst 档，这个 cliff 的意义被 E5 attention pruning 完全重新诠释：\n      - L2norm k=0.5 = 42.6% → attn_last k=0.5 = 99.2%（+56.6pp）\n      - 同样的 50 tokens，同样的 k=0.5（保留 25 tokens），attention 几乎完美而 L2norm catastrophic\n      - 因此 cliff 不是 \"BART encoder entanglement creates irreversible token dependencies\"，而是 \"L2norm 在 BART encoder 的 near-uniform norm distribution 上退化为 spatially clustered selection\"\n      - Reviewer argument：\"如果换 importance metric 就消除了 cliff，那 Axis-1 的 'token coupling' 定义有根本缺陷——关键不在 coupling 而在 importance metric。\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table H: X-VLA Cliff Zone — 3-Seed Deterministic\"\n        columns: [\"k\", \"L2norm SR(%)\", \"L2norm SD(pp)\", \"Random SR(%)\", \"Attn-Last SR(%)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0.90\", \"97.6\", \"—\", \"97.8\", \"~99\"]\n          - [\"0.85\", \"67.9\", \"0.31\", \"63.6\", \"~97\"]\n          - [\"0.80\", \"89.0\", \"0.72\", \"89.4\", \"~99\"]\n          - [\"0.70\", \"56.2\", \"—\", \"65.2\", \"99.2\"]\n          - [\"0.50\", \"42.6\", \"—\", \"70.6\", \"99.2\"]\n        notes: \"Attention pruning 完全消除 cliff 和 degradation。问题在 metric 不在 architecture。\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig X-VLA 3-method comparison: L2norm (cliff+degradation), Random (moderate degradation), Attention (near-flat). 三条 curve 在同一 plot 上，清晰展示 metric choice 的 decisive role。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cliff localization 数据本身是 solid experimental result。但在 worst 档，E5 data 完全改变其解读：\n      cliff 不是 connector architecture 的 intrinsic property，而是 L2norm importance metric 在 low-CV distribution 上的 pathological behavior。\n      Attention pruning（zero additional training）消除所有 degradation，这意味着 BART encoder 并没有 \"entangle\" tokens in a way that prevents pruning，它只是让 tokens 的 L2-norm 不再是 good importance proxy。\n      Paper 需要重新定义 Axis-1：从 \"token coupling\" 改为 \"importance metric suitability\"，或者承认 2-axis framework 是 L2norm-specific observation 而非 architecture-level insight。\n\n  - name: \"OFT CV Diagnostic (Token Importance Measurement)\"\n    plan_id: \"diagnostic_oft_cv\"\n    description: >\n      OpenVLA-OFT 的 token importance CV 测量。Expected CV≈0.219（≈Standard OpenVLA）。\n    expected_results:\n      oft_cv: 0.219\n      oft_cv_std: 0.012\n      oft_entropy: 0.667\n      openvla_standard_cv: 0.215\n      cv_delta_pp: 0.4\n      sr_eval_blocked: true\n      gpu_incompatibility: \"Blackwell SDPA requires A100+torch2.2\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      OFT CV=0.219 ≈ Standard OpenVLA CV=0.215（Δ=0.004），确认 connector（3-layer MLP）而非 action head（OFT vs standard）决定 token importance distribution。\n      Entropy 也几乎相同（0.667 vs 0.661）。这是 framework 的 positive confirmation——same connector → same CV → same predicted pruning behavior。\n      但在 worst 档，这个 data point 的价值有限：\n      (1) 无法在 LIBERO 上 eval SR（Blackwell GPU SDPA 不兼容），所以 CV 预测没有 ground truth 验证\n      (2) OFT 和 Standard OpenVLA 用相同 connector 产生相同 CV 是 trivially expected，不提供 additional discrimination power\n      (3) Reviewer 会指出：\"你们有 6 个 model 的 CV，但只有 4 个能实际 eval SR。CV 作为 predictor 的 validation set 太小。\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table I: Diagnostic Metrics — 6-Model Spectrum\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Connector\", \"CV\", \"Entropy\", \"Eval SR Available?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"π0\", \"Pure linear\", \"0.038\", \"0.959\", \"Offline only\"]\n          - [\"π0.5\", \"Pure linear (×√d)\", \"0.055\", \"—\", \"Yes (4 suites)\"]\n          - [\"X-VLA\", \"Linear + BART 12L\", \"0.151\", \"0.614\", \"Yes (4 suites)\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"3-layer MLP\", \"0.215\", \"0.661\", \"Yes (Object only)\"]\n          - [\"OFT\", \"3-layer MLP (DINOv2+SigLIP)\", \"0.219\", \"0.667\", \"No (GPU blocked)\"]\n          - [\"SmolVLA\", \"Pixel-shuffle\", \"0.314\", \"0.952\", \"Yes (4 suites)\"]\n        notes: \"6 models 有 CV，但仅 3 models 有 full cross-suite SR。OFT 和 π0 只有 diagnostic metrics。\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      OFT CV 完成了 6-model diagnostic table，但不改变任何结论。在 worst 档，这是 incrementally supportive 而非 decisive evidence。\n\n  - name: \"OFT Full Graded-Class Evaluation (4 Suites)\"\n    plan_id: \"c3_oft_graded_full\"\n    description: >\n      OpenVLA-OFT 在 4 个 LIBERO suites 上的 baseline + pruning evaluation。\n      worst 档：GPU 不兼容问题持续，无法完成 evaluation。\n    expected_results:\n      eval_blocked: true\n      blocker: \"Blackwell GPU SDPA incompatibility with OpenVLA-OFT\"\n      workaround_attempted: \"A100 rental, torch2.2 downgrade — both failed\"\n      fallback_evidence: \"CV=0.219≈OpenVLA, entropy=0.667≈0.661 — inferred graded behavior\"\n      paper_impact: \"Missing 2nd graded-class SR data point, relies on CV inference\"\n      reviewer_risk: \"Moderate — 2/3 connector classes have ≥2 SR-evaluated models, MLP class has only 1\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      OFT evaluation 在 worst 档仍然被 GPU 不兼容阻塞。Blackwell GPU 的 SDPA implementation 与 OFT checkpoint 的 torch 版本不兼容，降级 torch 或租用 A100 都不可行（timeline 限制）。\n      Paper 只能用 CV/entropy comparison 间接 argue OFT follows OpenVLA pattern。Reviewer 会注意到 MLP projector class 只有 OpenVLA 1 个 model 有 SR data，不足以 generalize。\n      CogACT（literature baseline, MLP projector, 74.8%→74.2% under 78% pruning from EfficientVLA）可以作为 external evidence，但不是 our own evaluation。\n      In worst tier, this is a clear gap but not fatal — pixel-shuffle (SmolVLA, 1 model, universal 0%) and linear (π0/π0.5, 2 models, variable) are well-characterized. MLP class has 1 internal + 1 external data point.\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Missing OFT SR data 在 worst 档是 acknowledged limitation。Reviewer concern 等级 \"moderate\"——不会 reject paper，但会要求 camera-ready 补充或更 cautious language about MLP class generalization。\n\n  - name: \"Perceiver Resampler (RoboFlamingo) — 3rd Connector Family\"\n    plan_id: \"c5_third_connector_roboflamingo\"\n    description: >\n      RoboFlamingo (Perceiver Resampler connector) 在 LIBERO 上 fine-tune + pruning。\n      worst 档：fine-tuning 产生低 baseline，且 Perceiver 不清晰地落入 2-axis taxonomy。\n    expected_results:\n      fine_tuning_baseline_sr_pct_predicted: 18.0\n      fine_tuning_difficulty: \"high — requires custom training pipeline adaptation\"\n      perceiver_cv_predicted: 0.28\n      perceiver_pruning_k09_predicted_sr_pct: 4.0\n      perceiver_pruning_k05_predicted_sr_pct: 0.0\n      taxonomy_fit: \"ambiguous — cross-attention creates partial entanglement different from both pixel-shuffle and BART\"\n      paper_inclusion: \"dropped — insufficient time and unclear taxonomy value\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      RoboFlamingo 在 worst 档面临多重困难：\n      (1) Fine-tuning infrastructure：RoboFlamingo 使用 Flamingo-style cross-attention perceiver resampler，将 variable-length vision tokens 压缩到 fixed 64 queries。这需要 custom training pipeline，previous attempts (train_c5_roboflamingo_v2) 被 killed。\n      (2) Low baseline：Perceiver Resampler 的 cross-attention 在 LIBERO manipulation tasks 上可能不如 direct projection（SmolVLA 59.2%, OpenVLA 74%），因为 LIBERO 需要 precise spatial information 而 perceiver 天然是 lossy compression。预测 baseline ~18% SR。\n      (3) Taxonomy ambiguity：Perceiver Resampler 的 cross-attention 与 BART encoder 的 self-attention 和 pixel-shuffle 的 spatial folding 都不同。它是 \"learned entanglement\" 而非 \"structural entanglement\"。CV 可能在 0.2-0.3 range，不清晰地落入现有 taxonomy。\n      (4) Timeline：距 abstract deadline 1 天，paper deadline 4 天，没有时间 debug fine-tuning pipeline + run full evaluation。\n      In worst tier, RoboFlamingo 被 dropped from paper。这减少了 paper 的 connector family 覆盖（3→2 confirmed families），但避免了 messy data 进一步复杂化已经 fragile 的 framework。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Dropping RoboFlamingo 在 worst 档是 rational choice：paper 已经有足够的 models（5 models × 4 suites）作为 empirical contribution，加入一个 low-baseline 的新 connector 只会模糊 narrative。\n      但这意味着 paper 的 connector 覆盖限于 linear/MLP/pixel-shuffle 三类，reviewer 可能指出 \"what about attention-based connectors (Perceiver, Q-Former)?\" 作为 limitation。\n\n  - name: \"VTR M-Sweep Completion (SmolVLA 3-seed × 5 M-values)\"\n    plan_id: \"c4_learned_reencoding_smolvla\"\n    description: >\n      SmolVLA VTR M-sweep 的 3-seed 完成和 MLP adapter control。\n      worst 档：数据 solid 但 M=96 dip 和 high variance 引起质疑。\n    expected_results:\n      m16_3seed_mean_sr_pct: 56.9\n      m16_3seed_std_pp: 1.3\n      m32_3seed_mean_sr_pct: 60.1\n      m32_3seed_std_pp: 1.3\n      m64_3seed_mean_sr_pct: 62.0\n      m64_3seed_std_pp: 2.3\n      m96_3seed_mean_sr_pct: 54.5\n      m96_3seed_std_pp: 3.2\n      m128_3seed_mean_sr_pct: 58.0\n      m128_3seed_std_pp: 3.5\n      mlp_adapter_m32_3seed_mean_sr_pct: 63.4\n      mlp_adapter_m32_3seed_std_pp: 2.6\n      vtc_vs_mlp_pvalue: 0.15\n      m64_vs_m96_pvalue: 0.034\n      baseline_sr_pct: 59.2\n      m_curve_flat_within_3pp: true\n      m96_dip_significant: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      VTR M-sweep 数据 intrinsically solid：M=16(56.9%) 到 M=128(58.0%) 都在 baseline 59.2% 的 ±5pp 内，证明 near-lossless compression at any ratio。MLP adapter control（63.4%）与 VTC（60.1%）无显著差异（p=0.15），确认 architecture independence。\n      但 worst 档关注两个 weakness：\n      (1) M=96 dip（54.5%, p=0.034 vs M=64=62.0%）虽然在 Bonferroni correction 后 marginally significant，但 3.2pp std 是所有 M 值中最高的。这暗示 training instability——某些 seed/M 组合在 training dynamics 中进入 suboptimal basin。\n      (2) M=128 passthrough 的 3.5pp std 也高，且 seed43=54.0% 是 outlier（其他两个 seed 59.8/60.2%）。如果 passthrough control 本身有 6pp variance，\"near-lossless\" 的声称需要 caveat。\n      In worst tier, VTR 仍然是 valid method（0%→~59% recovery），但 training stability concern 使其从 \"recommended practice\" 降级为 \"promising but needs further investigation\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table J: VTR M-Sweep 3-Seed Results\"\n        columns: [\"M\", \"Compression(%)\", \"Mean SR(%)\", \"Std(pp)\", \"Individual Seeds\", \"vs Baseline\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"16\", \"87.5\", \"56.9\", \"1.3\", \"55.8/58.4/56.5\", \"-2.3pp\"]\n          - [\"32\", \"75.0\", \"60.1\", \"1.3\", \"61.6/59.2/59.6\", \"+0.9pp\"]\n          - [\"64\", \"50.0\", \"62.0\", \"2.3\", \"61.6/60.0/64.4\", \"+2.8pp\"]\n          - [\"96\", \"25.0\", \"54.5\", \"3.2\", \"52.6/58.2/52.8\", \"-4.7pp\"]\n          - [\"128\", \"0.0\", \"58.0\", \"3.5\", \"59.8/54.0/60.2\", \"-1.2pp\"]\n          - [\"MLP-32\", \"75.0\", \"63.4\", \"2.6\", \"65.2/64.6/60.4\", \"+4.2pp\"]\n        notes: \"M=96 dip p=0.034。M=128 seed43=54.0 outlier。Flat M-curve 成立但 variance 在高 M 处增大。\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig M-curve with 3-seed error bars and baseline band (59.2%±3pp shaded). M=96 dip 和 M=128 variance clearly visible。\"\n    analysis: >\n      VTR 在 worst 档仍是 paper 的 positive contribution：hard pruning 0% → VTR ~59% ≈ baseline 是 dramatic recovery。\n      但 M=96 dip 和 high-M variance 需要 honest reporting。建议 paper 用 M=32 或 M=64 作为 recommended setting（stable seeds, good compression ratio），将 M=96 dip 作为 \"open question: why does M=96 underperform?\" 放入 discussion。\n      Reviewer concern level: low-moderate. VTR 的 core claim（recovery from 0% to baseline）is robust. M=96 是 interesting anomaly 但不 undermine main contribution。\n\n  - name: \"Consolidated Cross-Suite Framework Accuracy Assessment\"\n    plan_id: \"c6_libero_suite_expansion\"\n    description: >\n      综合所有 cross-suite 数据的 framework 准确率评估。\n      worst 档：framework accuracy ~62%，不足以支撑 \"principled framework\" 定位。\n    expected_results:\n      framework_predictions_total: 20\n      framework_predictions_correct: 12\n      framework_accuracy_pct: 62\n      claims_surviving_review: 2.5\n      surviving_claims: \"C2 (pixel-shuffle entanglement), C4 (VTR case study), partial C3b (MLP graded)\"\n      failed_claims: \"C1 (2-axis framework as principled theory), C5 (CV universal predictor)\"\n      reframed_claims: \"C1→empirical observation catalog, C5→within-suite heuristic\"\n      paper_contribution_type: \"empirical study with surprising findings\"\n      corl_submission_viable: true\n      corl_acceptance_probability_pct: 45\n    result_rationale: >\n      Framework accuracy 计算方法：\n      - SmolVLA × 4 suites: 预测 \"catastrophic at k=0.95\" → 实际 all suites ≤0.1% → 4/4 correct\n      - X-VLA × 4 suites: 预测 \"entangling, task-dependent collapse\" → Object OK (97.6%), Goal 70.2% (partial collapse), Spatial 78.8% (moderate), Long 27.5% (collapse) → 3/4 correct（Object 不 collapse，与预测不符）\n      - π0.5 × 4 suites: 预测 \"independent, immune to task complexity\" → Object random k=0.9=9%（NOT immune!），但 L2norm=98.2% → method-dependent → 1/4 correct（框架不区分 method）\n      - OpenVLA × 4 suites: 预测 \"graded, L2norm preferred\" → Object L2norm>random (+1.8pp ✓), Goal random>L2norm (+8.8pp ✗) → 2/4 correct\n      - π0 × offline: 预测 \"immune\" → k=0.1 improves → 1/1 correct\n      Total: 4+3+1+2+1 = 11/17 = 65%（≈62% with margin of error）\n\n      Claims survival analysis:\n      - C1 (2-axis framework): FAILS as theory → survives as \"descriptive taxonomy for L2norm pruning on Object suite\"\n      - C2 (pixel-shuffle entanglement): SURVIVES — universal 0% across all suites/methods/k is unambiguous\n      - C3a (linear proj depends on pipeline): Partially survives — π0 immune, π0.5 method-dependent, X-VLA cliff\n      - C3b (MLP graded): Survives on Object — graded curve confirmed\n      - C4 (VTR): Survives as SmolVLA case study — 0%→59% recovery\n      - C5 (CV predicts strategy): FAILS as universal law → survives as \"within-Object-suite heuristic\"\n\n      2.5 claims survive: C2, C4, half of C3b.\n\n      CoRL viability: paper 作为 \"comprehensive empirical study\" 仍然 viable（5 models × 4 suites × 3 methods 是任何 VLA pruning 工作中最大规模的 comparison）。Acceptance probability ~45%——足够好的 empirical contribution 但缺少 unified theory 会让某些 reviewers 觉得 \"incremental\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table K: Framework Prediction Accuracy by Model\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Connector Class\", \"Framework Prediction\", \"Object\", \"Spatial\", \"Goal\", \"Long\", \"Accuracy\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"SmolVLA\", \"Pixel-shuffle\", \"Catastrophic all suites\", \"✓\", \"✓\", \"✓\", \"✓\", \"4/4\"]\n          - [\"X-VLA\", \"BART encoder\", \"Task-dependent collapse\", \"✗(no collapse)\", \"✓\", \"✓\", \"✓\", \"3/4\"]\n          - [\"π0.5\", \"Linear proj\", \"Immune to task complexity\", \"✗(random cliff)\", \"✗\", \"✗\", \"✗\", \"1/4\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"MLP\", \"Graded, L2norm preferred\", \"✓\", \"~\", \"✗(random preferred)\", \"~\", \"2/4\"]\n          - [\"π0\", \"Linear proj\", \"Immune\", \"✓(offline)\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\", \"1/1\"]\n        notes: \"Total 11/17 ≈ 65%。π0.5 是 framework 最大 failure point。\"\n      - title: \"Table L: Claim Survival Assessment\"\n        columns: [\"Claim\", \"Original Status\", \"Worst-Tier Status\", \"Surviving Evidence\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"C1: 2-Axis Framework\", \"Primary contribution\", \"Fails as theory\", \"Descriptive taxonomy for L2norm-Object only\"]\n          - [\"C2: Pixel-Shuffle Entanglement\", \"Strong\", \"Survives\", \"Universal 0% across 4 suites × 2 methods\"]\n          - [\"C3: Connector-Specific Patterns\", \"Strong\", \"Partial survival\", \"MLP graded confirmed; linear 'immune' falsified\"]\n          - [\"C4: VTR Recovery\", \"Strong\", \"Survives as case study\", \"0%→59% on SmolVLA; fails on OpenVLA\"]\n          - [\"C5: CV Scaling Law\", \"Novel contribution\", \"Fails as universal\", \"Within-Object heuristic only; cross-suite |ρ|≈0.45\"]\n        notes: \"2-3 claims survive review intact. Paper viable as empirical study, not as theory paper.\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig framework accuracy heatmap: 5 models × 4 suites grid, color = (prediction correct / partially correct / wrong). Visual impact: scattered errors, no clean pattern.\"\n      - \"Fig revised paper narrative flow: from 'discover governing principle' to 'provide systematic benchmark + catalog surprising findings'.\"\n    analysis: >\n      在 worst 档，paper 的 identity 发生根本转变：\n      FROM: \"We discover a principled 2-axis framework governing VLA token compressibility\"\n      TO: \"We provide the first systematic study of token pruning across VLA architectures, revealing that pruning behavior is an irreducible function of (connector, method, k, task), not reducible to simple architectural rules\"\n\n      Key novel findings that survive independently of the framework:\n      (1) Pixel-shuffle entanglement is real and irreversible — this is a genuine architectural insight\n      (2) Importance metric selection matters more than connector architecture — supported by E5 attention data + π0.5 method divergence\n      (3) L2norm is actively harmful on low-CV models — 36pp gap on π0.5, 28pp on X-VLA at k=0.5 Object\n      (4) VTR achieves near-lossless compression for pixel-shuffle — 0%→59% at any M ratio\n\n      These 4 findings are individually publishable observations that together constitute a substantial empirical contribution for CoRL, even without a unified theory. Title: \"A Systematic Study of Token Pruning Strategies Across VLA Architectures.\"\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0a5ab60b-18ac-4b1d-b58b-ab75725b2ce1","total_cost_usd":1.8396012499999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":116713,"cache_read_input_tokens":627940,"output_tokens":27829,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":116713,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":27110,"cache_read_input_tokens":127511,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1043,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1043},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":100285,"outputTokens":26,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.100415,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":7,"outputTokens":27829,"cacheReadInputTokens":627940,"cacheCreationInputTokens":116713,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.73918625,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"ab82bff4-b6fd-465a-b5e2-3f23a1bb8d9e"}
